WEBVTT

1
00:00:56,041 --> 00:00:57,666
Long live Bata Bhai!

2
00:00:57,750 --> 00:00:59,458
{\an8}Long live Bata Bhai!

3
00:00:59,541 --> 00:01:01,291
{\an8}Long live Bata Bhai!

4
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:03,875
{\an8}- Kids!
- Long live Bata Bhai!

5
00:01:04,166 --> 00:01:09,208
{\an8}You've been sitting here
for quite a while now.

6
00:01:09,958 --> 00:01:14,625
{\an8}Swami Bata Bhai salutes you.

7
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:21,541
{\an8}So, what's today's chapter?

8
00:01:22,250 --> 00:01:23,166
{\an8}Disease.

9
00:01:23,250 --> 00:01:24,791
{\an8}I understand

10
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:29,083
{\an8}what you guys are trying to ask.

11
00:01:29,833 --> 00:01:32,541
{\an8}Till now, we've seen plenty of diseases

12
00:01:33,250 --> 00:01:37,208
{\an8}that our white-coat doctor buddies
have cured.

13
00:01:37,916 --> 00:01:40,166
{\an8}But there's one disease

14
00:01:40,583 --> 00:01:43,708
{\an8}for which we've never found a cure.

15
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:48,583
{\an8}And that disease is greed.

16
00:01:48,708 --> 00:01:50,000
{\an8}Hey, buddy!

17
00:01:50,250 --> 00:01:53,583
{\an8}Why are you making us rack our brains?

18
00:01:53,666 --> 00:01:56,916
{\an8}Everyone's come here
to watch <i>Dhamaal </i>and have some fun.

19
00:01:57,500 --> 00:01:59,541
{\an8}Once they watch <i>Dhamaal,</i>

20
00:01:59,625 --> 00:02:02,666
{\an8}they'll learn everything there is
to know about greed.

21
00:02:02,750 --> 00:02:05,625
{\an8}Kids, let me tell you something.

22
00:02:06,083 --> 00:02:09,333
{\an8}This story is also about
some greedy people,

23
00:02:09,875 --> 00:02:13,625
{\an8}and it began a hundred years ago.

24
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:16,625
{\an8}On a dark, stormy night,

25
00:02:16,958 --> 00:02:19,083
{\an8}<i>right in the middle of the sea,</i>

26
00:02:19,250 --> 00:02:22,500
{\an8}<i>a sea pirate named Shaitaan Singh,</i>

27
00:02:22,875 --> 00:02:25,000
{\an8}<i>in one massive action sequence,</i>

28
00:02:25,250 --> 00:02:29,083
{\an8}<i>beat up and killed dozens of Englishmen.</i>

29
00:02:29,333 --> 00:02:33,625
{\an8}<i>And then, he looted the treasure</i>
<i>of those greedy Englishmen.</i>

30
00:02:34,250 --> 00:02:37,333
{\an8}<i>He hid the treasure on an island</i>

31
00:02:37,416 --> 00:02:40,708
{\an8}<i>and drew up a map to it.</i>

32
00:02:41,333 --> 00:02:43,833
{\an8}<i>The Englishmen managed</i>
<i>to kill Shaitaan Singh,</i>

33
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:47,166
{\an8}but they never found that map.

34
00:02:47,708 --> 00:02:50,208
{\an8}Since then, to this day,

35
00:02:50,625 --> 00:02:53,250
{\an8}the map to that treasure
has been searched for

36
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:57,291
{\an8}by all kinds of greedy crooks
and cheaters.

37
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:20,416
Jheenga…

38
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:23,125
I can't see anything.

39
00:03:23,916 --> 00:03:25,958
Boss, remove the lid.

40
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:29,916
The lid.

41
00:03:34,125 --> 00:03:36,291
He's such a dimwit.

42
00:03:39,333 --> 00:03:41,583
I still can't see anything, Jheenga.

43
00:03:42,333 --> 00:03:43,208
Hey, dumbo!

44
00:03:43,833 --> 00:03:44,708
I mean the lid.

45
00:03:45,166 --> 00:03:46,500
Remove the binocular's lid.

46
00:03:46,625 --> 00:03:47,541
The lid.

47
00:03:51,916 --> 00:03:52,791
Yes, now see.

48
00:04:00,833 --> 00:04:02,708
- Leave me.
- Come on. We won't leave you.

49
00:04:02,791 --> 00:04:03,791
We will break your bones now.

50
00:04:10,166 --> 00:04:11,375
Finally, you're found.

51
00:04:12,166 --> 00:04:14,583
Now, tell me where the treasure map is?

52
00:04:14,916 --> 00:04:15,791
I won't tell you.

53
00:04:18,375 --> 00:04:19,250
Search him.

54
00:04:25,250 --> 00:04:26,958
Boss, he has a gun.

55
00:04:27,333 --> 00:04:30,083
If he has a gun,
he must have the map, too.

56
00:04:30,291 --> 00:04:31,833
Check again. Come on.

57
00:04:38,791 --> 00:04:39,666
- Boss!
- What?

58
00:04:39,916 --> 00:04:43,375
Your girlfriend Shabnam's photo
is in his wallet.

59
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:47,875
Shabbo?!

60
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:49,750
My Shabbo's photo…

61
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:52,500
How did you get it?

62
00:04:53,041 --> 00:04:53,916
Hey!

63
00:04:54,333 --> 00:04:57,166
Who else has
my Shabbo's photo?

64
00:04:59,208 --> 00:05:00,708
Tell me, who else has it?

65
00:05:01,666 --> 00:05:02,750
Who has her photo?

66
00:05:12,416 --> 00:05:14,541
Who else has my Shabbo…

67
00:05:20,250 --> 00:05:22,125
I will deal with you all later.

68
00:05:22,583 --> 00:05:23,458
Prithvi!

69
00:05:24,375 --> 00:05:25,541
I won't spare you now.

70
00:05:26,166 --> 00:05:27,041
Boss!

71
00:05:27,125 --> 00:05:29,000
Snatch away the map first
and then kill him.

72
00:05:29,083 --> 00:05:30,416
- Yeah.
- Hey, search him.

73
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:31,375
Hey…

74
00:05:31,458 --> 00:05:33,041
- Come here.
- Leave me.

75
00:05:33,125 --> 00:05:34,000
Check properly.

76
00:05:35,375 --> 00:05:37,166
- Boss, here's the map.
- Hey…

77
00:05:37,333 --> 00:05:41,333
Boss, presenting to you
the treasure map.

78
00:05:42,166 --> 00:05:44,166
Hey, found it.

79
00:05:45,416 --> 00:05:50,125
{\an8}Found the treasure map…

80
00:05:51,583 --> 00:05:54,416
Hey, I've found the treasure map.

81
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:56,875
- Return that map.
- Hey! Back off!

82
00:05:58,458 --> 00:06:01,125
To get this map, my heart was…

83
00:06:01,208 --> 00:06:02,333
Fire! Fire!

84
00:06:02,416 --> 00:06:06,541
Yes, my heart was burning
with a fire no one could put out.

85
00:06:06,750 --> 00:06:08,875
Idiot! Is he mentally unstable?

86
00:06:08,958 --> 00:06:09,875
Since birth!

87
00:06:10,166 --> 00:06:12,250
Boss, we need to put out this fire.

88
00:06:12,333 --> 00:06:15,208
And who are you to put out my fire?

89
00:06:15,291 --> 00:06:16,291
No one can extinguish this fire…

90
00:06:17,250 --> 00:06:18,125
Fire!

91
00:06:23,958 --> 00:06:26,083
My map got burnt because of you.

92
00:06:26,458 --> 00:06:27,416
I won't spare you.

93
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:29,000
Hey, half-brain!

94
00:06:29,791 --> 00:06:30,875
You can't kill me.

95
00:06:31,291 --> 00:06:32,833
Because the map
is stored in my memory.

96
00:06:33,208 --> 00:06:35,791
And I won't… share it with you.

97
00:06:36,041 --> 00:06:37,166
Then I will also…

98
00:06:39,041 --> 00:06:40,166
torture you.

99
00:06:44,416 --> 00:06:45,291
Did you feel the pain?

100
00:06:45,750 --> 00:06:48,125
Yes, sir.

101
00:07:01,041 --> 00:07:03,625
There comes my friend.

102
00:07:09,458 --> 00:07:12,250
There goes your friend.

103
00:07:14,083 --> 00:07:15,083
Fire!

104
00:07:16,541 --> 00:07:18,083
He shouldn't be spared.

105
00:07:18,416 --> 00:07:19,291
Don't leave him.

106
00:07:19,833 --> 00:07:20,833
Kill him.

107
00:07:21,291 --> 00:07:22,166
Yes!

108
00:07:22,458 --> 00:07:26,041
Hey, blind fellow, aim with this eye.
Where's he?

109
00:07:55,250 --> 00:07:57,625
I knew you would come to rescue me.

110
00:07:57,708 --> 00:07:58,708
I didn't come here to rescue you.

111
00:07:59,041 --> 00:08:00,083
I came to punish you.

112
00:08:00,750 --> 00:08:03,541
Idiot, I gave you the map to decode,

113
00:08:03,791 --> 00:08:06,291
but your greed got the better of you,
and you double-crossed me and ran away?

114
00:08:06,375 --> 00:08:08,958
But bro,
I'm the one who called you here.

115
00:08:09,291 --> 00:08:11,250
You called me
because you sensed danger.

116
00:08:11,875 --> 00:08:14,333
Don't touch my family jewel.

117
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:15,375
Where's the map?

118
00:08:15,458 --> 00:08:16,333
It got burned.

119
00:08:16,416 --> 00:08:17,666
- What?!
- Don't worry.

120
00:08:17,833 --> 00:08:20,125
The whole map is stored in my memory.
I will share every detail with you.

121
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:22,666
But first, find a way
to get us out of here, bro.

122
00:08:22,833 --> 00:08:26,583
I'm begging you. Please,
get me out of this place safely.

123
00:08:26,666 --> 00:08:27,541
- Boss.
- Yes.

124
00:08:27,708 --> 00:08:28,583
He's there.

125
00:08:29,041 --> 00:08:30,458
Hey, catch them.

126
00:08:30,708 --> 00:08:31,916
- Hey.
- Catch them.

127
00:08:32,458 --> 00:08:33,375
Make sure they don't run away.

128
00:08:33,833 --> 00:08:35,416
Leave me.

129
00:08:38,875 --> 00:08:39,791
Hey!

130
00:08:40,083 --> 00:08:41,541
Nobody interferes.

131
00:08:42,416 --> 00:08:44,166
He's my prey.

132
00:08:44,416 --> 00:08:45,375
Okay, boss.

133
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:50,208
I'll blow up your head with my gun.

134
00:08:58,458 --> 00:08:59,333
Leave him.

135
00:09:08,250 --> 00:09:09,958
Boss! Careful!

136
00:09:12,250 --> 00:09:14,541
Remember what your boss said?
Nobody interferes.

137
00:09:14,625 --> 00:09:15,833
I'm the boss.

138
00:09:16,250 --> 00:09:17,250
I cancel my own order.

139
00:09:17,375 --> 00:09:18,291
Beat him up.

140
00:09:18,375 --> 00:09:19,250
Hit him!

141
00:09:21,333 --> 00:09:23,125
Leave… leave me.

142
00:09:23,708 --> 00:09:25,375
Leave me. Leave me.

143
00:09:25,750 --> 00:09:28,583
- Hey, blow air.
- Where?

144
00:09:28,666 --> 00:09:30,000
In my eyes!

145
00:09:30,208 --> 00:09:31,083
I'm doing it.

146
00:09:52,750 --> 00:09:54,416
Take out your knife, come on.

147
00:09:54,500 --> 00:09:56,958
Come on, aim.
Aim at him.

148
00:09:57,125 --> 00:09:58,333
Aim for his chest.

149
00:10:04,791 --> 00:10:05,666
Jheenga!

150
00:10:05,875 --> 00:10:06,833
- Jheenga!
- Yes.

151
00:10:07,125 --> 00:10:08,958
- Look at that pink pigeon.
- Where?

152
00:10:12,666 --> 00:10:13,541
You tricked me.

153
00:10:16,666 --> 00:10:17,541
Eyepatch!

154
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,208
- Now, have fun.
- Coconut.

155
00:10:22,291 --> 00:10:23,166
Boss, pull it out.

156
00:10:23,250 --> 00:10:24,916
Yes, I will.
I can't stand the sight of blood.

157
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:25,875
Wait a second.

158
00:10:25,958 --> 00:10:26,833
It's out!

159
00:10:54,125 --> 00:10:55,000
Hold me.

160
00:10:59,291 --> 00:11:00,166
What a relief!

161
00:11:02,833 --> 00:11:05,708
- Bye!
- Hey!

162
00:11:14,125 --> 00:11:16,208
Cannon. Cannon.
Stop limping and run.

163
00:11:18,583 --> 00:11:20,666
Hey, idiot!
Load it into the cannon.

164
00:11:23,416 --> 00:11:25,250
- Light it!
- What to light?

165
00:11:25,375 --> 00:11:26,375
Light the fuse.

166
00:11:30,375 --> 00:11:32,583
Sorry, Guddu!

167
00:11:33,333 --> 00:11:36,041
- Yes, turn it to the center. Center.
- Hit him.

168
00:11:36,125 --> 00:11:37,875
Left… left! Fire!

169
00:11:37,958 --> 00:11:39,125
Make sure to blow him into pieces.

170
00:11:44,958 --> 00:11:46,916
Boss, the cannonball is going upward.

171
00:11:58,208 --> 00:12:00,166
Boss, it's coming back down.

172
00:12:07,416 --> 00:12:08,291
It's hot.

173
00:12:09,291 --> 00:12:10,166
It's hot.

174
00:12:23,791 --> 00:12:27,000
This will explode. We will die.

175
00:12:30,666 --> 00:12:31,583
A cannonball…

176
00:12:59,250 --> 00:13:00,250
<i>It's missing.</i>

177
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:01,666
<i>Who's missing?</i>

178
00:13:01,750 --> 00:13:03,416
<i>The "H" is missing.</i>

179
00:13:03,500 --> 00:13:05,000
<i>Oh. Sorry, bro.</i>

180
00:13:05,958 --> 00:13:07,083
<i>Here comes the "H".</i>

181
00:13:08,625 --> 00:13:10,375
<i>Not there.</i>
<i>Place it after "D".</i>

182
00:13:10,458 --> 00:13:11,500
<i>Sorry again.</i>

183
00:13:11,875 --> 00:13:13,291
<i>I'll fix it right away.</i>

184
00:13:14,125 --> 00:13:15,500
<i>Here comes the "H".</i>

185
00:13:46,375 --> 00:13:50,916
Bro. Sorry to inform you
that you're no longer alive.

186
00:13:51,125 --> 00:13:52,666
Rest in peace.

187
00:13:55,750 --> 00:13:56,708
Put that to your ear?

188
00:13:56,916 --> 00:13:59,375
You've already slapped me.
Still, if you insist…

189
00:14:01,333 --> 00:14:02,916
I told you to put this to your ear,
the stethoscope.

190
00:14:03,083 --> 00:14:05,041
That's not necessary.
I have good news for you.

191
00:14:05,125 --> 00:14:07,583
You're alive.

192
00:14:07,916 --> 00:14:09,875
No. I want Prithvi.

193
00:14:10,250 --> 00:14:11,333
I want the secret of the treasure.

194
00:14:11,625 --> 00:14:12,625
Until then,
there's no good news for me.

195
00:14:12,750 --> 00:14:14,750
No, listen. I've sent Mannu Makoda

196
00:14:14,833 --> 00:14:17,500
to Prithvi's house at Chamboli Ghat.

197
00:14:17,708 --> 00:14:20,916
He will come there to meet his girlfriend,
and we will grab him there.

198
00:14:22,083 --> 00:14:25,000
- I want Prithvi.
- Bro, blood pressure…

199
00:14:25,208 --> 00:14:27,083
- I want Prithvi.
- Your blood pressure…

200
00:14:27,166 --> 00:14:31,916
- I want Prithvi.
- Bro. Your blood pressure is shooting up.

201
00:14:39,916 --> 00:14:43,291
Bro, I'm such an amazing doctor.
It's getting under control now.

202
00:14:54,958 --> 00:14:58,416
Oh… here comes his ICU.

203
00:15:11,583 --> 00:15:12,500
Guddu!

204
00:15:13,625 --> 00:15:14,500
What happened to you?

205
00:15:15,291 --> 00:15:16,916
The same thing that happens every
time I see you.

206
00:15:19,958 --> 00:15:22,208
After seeing you,
I can't notice anything else at all.

207
00:15:24,291 --> 00:15:25,166
Okay, listen.

208
00:15:25,250 --> 00:15:26,541
I've already spoken with the kids.

209
00:15:26,958 --> 00:15:28,916
Come and meet them in the evening.

210
00:15:29,333 --> 00:15:30,833
If the kids like you,

211
00:15:31,166 --> 00:15:32,500
then our family will be complete.

212
00:15:33,083 --> 00:15:35,750
If I've already won the mother,
then the kids are…

213
00:15:36,750 --> 00:15:37,625
What?

214
00:15:38,541 --> 00:15:40,041
I'll win them, too.

215
00:15:47,708 --> 00:15:48,791
Hey, Lord Krishna!

216
00:15:49,291 --> 00:15:50,208
Goddess Radha!

217
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:52,000
{\an8}Always have Your blessings on me.

218
00:15:52,083 --> 00:15:53,416
{\an8}DONATION BOX

219
00:15:53,500 --> 00:15:54,375
{\an8}God,

220
00:15:55,166 --> 00:15:58,166
{\an8}You already know that I'm not
the greedy type of person.

221
00:15:58,666 --> 00:15:59,875
{\an8}Anyway, what more do I even want?

222
00:16:00,291 --> 00:16:01,166
{\an8}What do I want?

223
00:16:01,500 --> 00:16:03,583
{\an8}Just a beautiful girl,

224
00:16:04,250 --> 00:16:07,125
{\an8}whose father owns
an extra-large bungalow,

225
00:16:07,833 --> 00:16:10,333
an extra-large car,

226
00:16:11,041 --> 00:16:13,916
an extra-large bank balance.

227
00:16:14,375 --> 00:16:17,083
And after marriage,
all of that should simply become mine!

228
00:16:17,416 --> 00:16:18,833
That's all I want.

229
00:16:20,500 --> 00:16:21,416
And for that,

230
00:16:21,666 --> 00:16:24,625
I'll offer five lakh rupees as
a donation to You, God.

231
00:16:24,958 --> 00:16:27,625
And yes, I've even brought
an advance payment.

232
00:16:28,791 --> 00:16:31,166
Fifty whole rupees from me.

233
00:16:31,291 --> 00:16:32,500
You'll definitely remember me for this!

234
00:16:46,916 --> 00:16:47,791
{\an8}God!

235
00:16:48,458 --> 00:16:50,750
{\an8}You've accepted
the request so quickly!

236
00:16:52,375 --> 00:16:53,625
{\an8}Do You have a 5G network?

237
00:17:04,333 --> 00:17:05,583
You took my "extra-large" request

238
00:17:06,166 --> 00:17:07,625
quite seriously.

239
00:17:10,041 --> 00:17:11,541
It's an extra-large car.

240
00:17:15,833 --> 00:17:17,875
Well, I can adjust to that much.

241
00:17:18,416 --> 00:17:20,916
But God, You should also adjust a little.

242
00:17:21,333 --> 00:17:25,333
I'll pay this 50 rupees along
with the full and final payment.

243
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:33,500
Why are you getting so angry, God?

244
00:17:38,833 --> 00:17:42,125
Seth, when are you getting
your daughter Paro married?

245
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:48,125
Seth <i>ji,</i> every father worries
about his daughter's marriage.

246
00:17:49,375 --> 00:17:50,291
I'm worried too.

247
00:17:51,458 --> 00:17:53,000
With God's grace,
she will get married very soon.

248
00:17:57,500 --> 00:18:00,000
Thank you for dropping me
off at the temple, Uncle.

249
00:18:00,541 --> 00:18:02,000
- Bye, Dad.
- Bless you, dear.

250
00:18:02,750 --> 00:18:03,791
Go safely.

251
00:18:55,208 --> 00:18:57,666
Sorry. I hope you aren't hurt.

252
00:18:59,250 --> 00:19:00,250
Not really.

253
00:19:01,125 --> 00:19:02,541
But this heart did feel something.

254
00:19:02,833 --> 00:19:03,833
What…

255
00:19:04,708 --> 00:19:05,666
what's going on?

256
00:19:08,250 --> 00:19:09,625
Now, I'm hurt.

257
00:19:12,666 --> 00:19:13,958
But it's the sweet feeling.

258
00:19:16,291 --> 00:19:17,166
Natthu.

259
00:19:19,166 --> 00:19:20,291
Hey, Natthu.

260
00:19:20,791 --> 00:19:21,958
- Did you notice?
- Yes.

261
00:19:22,125 --> 00:19:24,458
I've enticed Seth's daughter.

262
00:19:25,250 --> 00:19:26,958
No, Lallan, he's Seth.

263
00:19:27,166 --> 00:19:28,666
But he's the d…

264
00:19:28,791 --> 00:19:31,000
No need to be afraid of anyone.

265
00:19:31,208 --> 00:19:33,208
When one has fallen in love,
then why fear?

266
00:19:33,291 --> 00:19:34,166
And take this.

267
00:19:34,416 --> 00:19:35,958
Distribute it to the poor on my behalf.

268
00:19:36,041 --> 00:19:36,916
You also take some.

269
00:19:37,208 --> 00:19:38,083
But…

270
00:19:39,083 --> 00:19:39,958
money?

271
00:19:44,708 --> 00:19:46,791
We were so happy on our wedding day.

272
00:19:47,208 --> 00:19:48,375
I love you, Rosy.

273
00:19:48,958 --> 00:19:51,041
Thank you for coming back into my life.

274
00:19:51,125 --> 00:19:52,791
Thank you.

275
00:19:59,625 --> 00:20:01,416
Adi, I will also play cricket.

276
00:20:04,500 --> 00:20:05,375
Cricket?

277
00:20:05,541 --> 00:20:07,583
You already took my wicket a year ago.

278
00:20:07,958 --> 00:20:09,583
My Rosy left me.

279
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:13,625
I've been living like a widow
for the past year.

280
00:20:13,916 --> 00:20:15,958
It's called a widower.

281
00:20:16,041 --> 00:20:17,500
Be it a widower or a widow.
How does it matter?

282
00:20:17,583 --> 00:20:18,791
No worries.

283
00:20:19,208 --> 00:20:21,208
Do you remember
what you did on my wedding night?

284
00:20:21,666 --> 00:20:22,541
Do you?

285
00:20:23,041 --> 00:20:24,583
Flashback will be here and not there.

286
00:20:24,708 --> 00:20:25,583
Sorry.

287
00:20:51,291 --> 00:20:52,583
Surprise!

288
00:20:53,166 --> 00:20:54,375
What are you doing here?

289
00:20:54,666 --> 00:20:56,875
I was hiding below the bed.
To surprise <i>bhabhi.</i>

290
00:20:56,958 --> 00:20:58,416
Is this how you should surprise…

291
00:20:58,541 --> 00:20:59,541
Couldn't you come in the morning?

292
00:20:59,750 --> 00:21:01,250
Adi, you're not so smart.

293
00:21:01,333 --> 00:21:02,583
One can't declare
the surprise beforehand.

294
00:21:02,666 --> 00:21:04,583
- Fire! Fire!
- Take this…

295
00:21:04,833 --> 00:21:06,541
Fire! Fire!

296
00:21:06,750 --> 00:21:07,708
Adi, please put out this fire.

297
00:21:07,791 --> 00:21:08,666
I'm trying.

298
00:21:08,791 --> 00:21:10,666
Manav, bring water. Quick.

299
00:21:10,750 --> 00:21:11,750
Water! Water!

300
00:21:13,708 --> 00:21:15,625
- Adi, please do something.
- Yes, I'm doing it.

301
00:21:16,208 --> 00:21:17,541
Adi, water.

302
00:21:17,625 --> 00:21:18,833
Throw water on <i>bhabhi.</i>

303
00:21:19,125 --> 00:21:20,458
Manav, throw water quickly.

304
00:21:25,166 --> 00:21:26,208
What have you done?

305
00:21:26,291 --> 00:21:27,500
You told me to throw water.

306
00:21:27,708 --> 00:21:29,083
Should you have thrown it on her face?

307
00:21:29,166 --> 00:21:30,041
Look at her now.

308
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:37,458
She left that day.

309
00:21:38,083 --> 00:21:39,166
And never returned.

310
00:21:39,375 --> 00:21:41,666
Adi, I am not so smart.

311
00:21:41,958 --> 00:21:42,833
I know.

312
00:21:43,916 --> 00:21:46,208
- Stop crying and listen carefully.
- Okay.

313
00:21:46,500 --> 00:21:48,291
I've told Rosy that my leg is fractured.

314
00:21:48,500 --> 00:21:49,500
She's coming to see me.

315
00:21:49,791 --> 00:21:52,708
I will make her so emotional

316
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:54,458
that she will never leave me again.

317
00:21:54,708 --> 00:21:56,708
Adi, you're so smart.

318
00:21:56,833 --> 00:21:57,708
I know.

319
00:21:57,791 --> 00:21:59,708
<i>Rogue! What did you say?</i>

320
00:21:59,833 --> 00:22:00,708
{\an8}<i>You don't keep change?</i>

321
00:22:00,791 --> 00:22:03,250
<i>- Bhabhi </i>is here. <i>Bhabhi </i>is here.
- Yes.

322
00:22:03,333 --> 00:22:05,000
<i>- Bhabhi…</i>
- You don't have the change, do you?

323
00:22:05,250 --> 00:22:06,416
Why don't you keep any change?

324
00:22:06,500 --> 00:22:08,250
- Sorry, madam.
- Get lost! I don't want your "sorry".

325
00:22:09,750 --> 00:22:10,750
She's such a dangerous woman.

326
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:12,250
- Let's go, Manav.
- Yes.

327
00:22:12,541 --> 00:22:14,166
Sit there and enjoy the walnut.
Just don't do anything.

328
00:22:14,250 --> 00:22:15,125
Okay.

329
00:22:35,125 --> 00:22:36,708
Enough. Stop crying.

330
00:22:37,833 --> 00:22:38,750
How did this happen?

331
00:22:38,875 --> 00:22:42,375
I was lost in your memories
while boarding a bus.

332
00:22:42,958 --> 00:22:44,625
Didn't realize when the bus crushed me.

333
00:22:46,041 --> 00:22:47,333
Since then, I've been in bed.

334
00:22:47,833 --> 00:22:48,833
All alone.

335
00:22:49,291 --> 00:22:50,166
Lonely.

336
00:22:50,625 --> 00:22:51,625
Helpless.

337
00:22:52,333 --> 00:22:54,458
- Don't leave me alone, Rosy.
- Enough.

338
00:22:54,791 --> 00:22:55,666
I've come back, right?

339
00:22:56,125 --> 00:22:57,541
Now I will stay here with you.

340
00:22:57,833 --> 00:23:00,166
Thank you. Thank you, Rosy.

341
00:23:00,250 --> 00:23:01,250
Alright! It's okay.

342
00:23:02,916 --> 00:23:03,791
Stupid!

343
00:23:03,875 --> 00:23:04,750
Keep that weight down.

344
00:23:04,833 --> 00:23:05,708
Okay.

345
00:23:08,250 --> 00:23:09,166
Oh no!

346
00:23:14,666 --> 00:23:15,916
Manav, what have you done?

347
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:17,416
I was trying to break the walnut.

348
00:23:17,500 --> 00:23:19,000
But you've hurt your <i>bhabhi </i>instead.

349
00:23:19,500 --> 00:23:20,833
I'm not so smart.

350
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,166
Manav, you idiot!

351
00:23:22,750 --> 00:23:23,625
<i>Bhabhi!</i>

352
00:23:23,708 --> 00:23:24,708
- Manav…
- Give this to me.

353
00:23:24,791 --> 00:23:25,666
Walnut! Walnut!

354
00:23:25,833 --> 00:23:26,708
Manav!

355
00:23:26,791 --> 00:23:28,500
- Leave it!
- This walnut.

356
00:23:31,833 --> 00:23:32,708
My walnut!

357
00:23:34,833 --> 00:23:35,875
Adi, it fell.

358
00:23:35,958 --> 00:23:37,666
It fell?! She fell!

359
00:23:37,833 --> 00:23:39,875
No, I mean the walnut fell.

360
00:23:39,958 --> 00:23:41,375
To hell with your walnut.

361
00:23:41,625 --> 00:23:43,291
Pull your <i>bhabhi </i>up. Come on.

362
00:23:43,958 --> 00:23:45,958
Yes! Yes!
<i>Bhabhi,</i> don't worry.

363
00:23:46,250 --> 00:23:47,125
Be happy!

364
00:23:47,375 --> 00:23:49,041
- Adi! Adi, what should I do?
- Pull up.

365
00:23:51,375 --> 00:23:52,583
Down! Down!

366
00:23:53,083 --> 00:23:54,291
Oh no!

367
00:23:57,125 --> 00:23:58,916
<i>Bhabhi.</i> Don't worry.

368
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:00,208
What are you doing?

369
00:24:00,458 --> 00:24:01,791
Are you pulling water from the well?

370
00:24:01,875 --> 00:24:04,083
- Pull your <i>bhabhi </i>up. Come on.
- Manav!

371
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:07,041
<i>Bhabhi,</i> don't worry.

372
00:24:22,375 --> 00:24:24,166
Oh no. <i>Bhabhi!</i>

373
00:24:24,250 --> 00:24:26,125
<i>- Bhabhi! Bhabhi!</i>
- Pull me up.

374
00:24:26,208 --> 00:24:27,541
- Don't worry.
- What are you doing?

375
00:24:27,625 --> 00:24:28,500
Hey, you!

376
00:24:30,083 --> 00:24:31,000
Keep it up, <i>bhabhi.</i>

377
00:24:31,083 --> 00:24:32,166
Yes. Very good.

378
00:24:35,916 --> 00:24:38,750
<i>- Bhabhi!</i> Are you alright, <i>bhabhi?</i>
- Are you fine?

379
00:24:39,250 --> 00:24:40,125
- Are you alright?
- Are you alright?

380
00:24:41,208 --> 00:24:42,791
How are you standing on your feet?

381
00:24:44,625 --> 00:24:46,000
It's a miracle!

382
00:24:46,125 --> 00:24:47,875
- It's a miracle!
- Miracle!

383
00:24:47,958 --> 00:24:49,958
- It's a miracle!
- It's a miracle!

384
00:24:50,125 --> 00:24:52,750
- Praise the Lord! Hallelujah!
- Hallelujah!

385
00:24:52,833 --> 00:24:54,000
- Adi!
- What happened?

386
00:24:54,916 --> 00:24:55,958
Which of your legs was broken?

387
00:24:56,041 --> 00:24:57,041
The right leg, <i>bhabhi.</i>

388
00:24:57,125 --> 00:24:58,291
- The right leg.
- Okay.

389
00:24:58,541 --> 00:25:00,541
And the plaster is there.
It's really…

390
00:25:00,625 --> 00:25:01,500
What are you doing?

391
00:25:02,958 --> 00:25:03,875
Shit! Shit!

392
00:25:08,541 --> 00:25:09,416
What happened?

393
00:25:19,916 --> 00:25:20,791
This is the one, bro?

394
00:25:21,416 --> 00:25:22,291
Press the bell.

395
00:25:42,791 --> 00:25:43,833
Bro!

396
00:25:52,750 --> 00:25:53,666
Bro!

397
00:25:56,041 --> 00:25:57,083
Automatic!

398
00:26:20,458 --> 00:26:21,875
- Bro…
- Yeah.

399
00:26:23,125 --> 00:26:24,583
Are you sure this
is <i>bhabhi's</i> house?

400
00:26:26,250 --> 00:26:28,250
Don't know.
I've also come here for the first time.

401
00:26:29,416 --> 00:26:30,291
Aaliya!

402
00:26:32,416 --> 00:26:34,541
Bro, I can't see anything.

403
00:26:34,666 --> 00:26:36,125
- Electricity went off, man.
- Okay.

404
00:26:36,208 --> 00:26:37,083
Aaliya!

405
00:26:37,666 --> 00:26:38,541
Aaliya!

406
00:26:39,083 --> 00:26:40,000
Aaliya…

407
00:26:42,083 --> 00:26:43,125
Hey, open the door.

408
00:26:43,625 --> 00:26:45,625
Somebody, please, open the door.

409
00:26:45,708 --> 00:26:47,458
But who closed the door?

410
00:26:47,541 --> 00:26:49,583
The one who opened it
must have closed it.

411
00:26:50,166 --> 00:26:51,333
Don't scare me, bro.

412
00:26:54,583 --> 00:26:55,458
Aaliya!

413
00:26:56,833 --> 00:26:57,708
Aaila!

414
00:26:58,750 --> 00:26:59,625
Aaila!

415
00:26:59,708 --> 00:27:00,875
Who's this Aaila, bro?

416
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:03,250
- It's Aaliya.
- Yes, yes. Aaliya.

417
00:27:03,458 --> 00:27:04,333
Aaliya <i>bhabhi!</i>

418
00:27:04,416 --> 00:27:05,750
Aaliya!

419
00:27:06,041 --> 00:27:07,291
- Aaliya <i>bhabhi!</i>
- Bro!

420
00:27:08,416 --> 00:27:09,333
Bro!

421
00:27:34,166 --> 00:27:35,041
Bro, no.

422
00:27:37,291 --> 00:27:38,166
No, bro.

423
00:27:55,166 --> 00:27:56,041
Bro!

424
00:28:00,083 --> 00:28:01,833
Are you sure this is <i>bhabhi's </i>house?

425
00:28:19,541 --> 00:28:21,875
Bro, underwear ghost.

426
00:28:25,416 --> 00:28:26,333
Not "underwear" ghost.

427
00:28:27,375 --> 00:28:28,541
It's an undercover ghost.

428
00:28:28,625 --> 00:28:29,916
Yes, exactly.

429
00:28:57,833 --> 00:28:58,833
Are you tired?

430
00:28:59,916 --> 00:29:01,666
Want some tea, brother?

431
00:29:02,500 --> 00:29:06,291
Less sugar, along
with some biscuits, sister.

432
00:29:06,916 --> 00:29:07,833
Right, bro?

433
00:29:08,583 --> 00:29:12,916
- Hey, run! Run!
- Run! Run!

434
00:29:13,500 --> 00:29:17,333
- Aaliya! Aaliya!
- Open the door, please.

435
00:29:18,041 --> 00:29:20,083
Anyone here?

436
00:29:20,666 --> 00:29:25,041
- Open the door! Open the door!
- Please, help us!

437
00:29:25,500 --> 00:29:26,958
Open the door!

438
00:29:27,333 --> 00:29:28,833
Hey…

439
00:29:32,708 --> 00:29:33,583
What happened, bro?

440
00:29:33,666 --> 00:29:35,291
Did you find the way out?

441
00:29:37,083 --> 00:29:38,625
We are done for real.

442
00:29:52,958 --> 00:29:54,125
Let us go.

443
00:29:56,333 --> 00:30:00,333
She's the Burj Khalifa of ghosts.

444
00:30:00,875 --> 00:30:04,291
You wanted to have some tea.
Right, bro?

445
00:30:05,000 --> 00:30:08,500
Elder sister is coming
with the biscuits.

446
00:30:12,666 --> 00:30:16,000
No. No, biscuits. Bread will do.

447
00:30:23,625 --> 00:30:25,875
Sister, you got long hands.

448
00:30:26,083 --> 00:30:27,583
Please, open the latch.

449
00:30:47,375 --> 00:30:48,250
Bro.

450
00:30:48,541 --> 00:30:49,875
She has a hearing problem.

451
00:30:49,958 --> 00:30:53,166
I told her to open the lock,
but she has handed over her head.

452
00:30:58,166 --> 00:31:01,041
No! Run, run, run, run!

453
00:31:02,250 --> 00:31:04,458
Here you go.
Have some tea and biscuits.

454
00:31:05,333 --> 00:31:06,583
Take it, brother.

455
00:31:07,291 --> 00:31:08,166
Take it.

456
00:31:08,416 --> 00:31:09,625
Okay, sister.

457
00:31:09,958 --> 00:31:10,833
Take it.

458
00:31:11,416 --> 00:31:12,375
Run!

459
00:31:12,458 --> 00:31:13,958
- Tea and biscuits.
- Sorry…

460
00:31:14,041 --> 00:31:16,375
- Let's run away.
- Bro…

461
00:31:16,583 --> 00:31:19,750
- Come on, bro!
- Run! Quick!

462
00:31:19,833 --> 00:31:21,125
- Run…
- Bro, come fast.

463
00:31:21,208 --> 00:31:22,958
We will jump from the terrace. Run, bro!

464
00:31:26,458 --> 00:31:27,416
Bro!

465
00:31:33,666 --> 00:31:35,708
Bro! Bro! Bro!

466
00:31:40,041 --> 00:31:41,250
- Ghost!
- Ghost!

467
00:31:42,166 --> 00:31:43,791
- Ghost!
- Ghost!

468
00:31:44,791 --> 00:31:45,916
- Aaliya!
- Guddu?!

469
00:31:46,083 --> 00:31:46,958
There's a ghost in this house.

470
00:31:47,041 --> 00:31:50,125
Yes! The ghost that serves tea
and sweeps the floor.

471
00:31:50,208 --> 00:31:51,791
You guys are looking like ghosts.

472
00:31:53,958 --> 00:31:55,541
No. There's a ghost in this house.

473
00:31:55,916 --> 00:31:58,333
No one is here except
Gangubai and my kids.

474
00:31:58,666 --> 00:31:59,541
Didn't they meet you?

475
00:32:02,125 --> 00:32:03,000
Kids.

476
00:32:05,083 --> 00:32:06,333
Hide it. Hurry up.

477
00:32:06,916 --> 00:32:07,791
Kids?

478
00:32:08,458 --> 00:32:10,541
- Hurry up, kids. Your mom is calling you.
- Yes.

479
00:32:20,541 --> 00:32:23,666
Dad, whether it's Guddu or anyone else,

480
00:32:24,666 --> 00:32:26,125
no one can ever replace you.

481
00:32:26,958 --> 00:32:27,833
No one.

482
00:32:29,291 --> 00:32:31,750
Go freshen up.
I'll send the kids to you.

483
00:32:32,333 --> 00:32:35,583
But remember,
you've got to impress them, okay?

484
00:32:37,041 --> 00:32:37,916
Kids!

485
00:32:39,041 --> 00:32:40,750
- Namaste!
- Namaste!

486
00:32:40,916 --> 00:32:44,166
Bro… they're so well-behaved!

487
00:32:45,750 --> 00:32:46,750
Not well-behaved.

488
00:32:47,708 --> 00:32:48,916
These kids are a menace.

489
00:32:50,041 --> 00:32:51,833
They had set up the horror treatment.

490
00:32:52,416 --> 00:32:53,291
Really?

491
00:32:54,708 --> 00:32:55,583
Aren't you ashamed?

492
00:32:56,125 --> 00:32:58,291
You turned your soon-to-be pop
into popcorn?

493
00:33:00,708 --> 00:33:03,833
But why did you do
this surgical strike on us?

494
00:33:04,125 --> 00:33:07,083
Because a third-class person like you,
who deals in second-class things,

495
00:33:07,166 --> 00:33:09,708
can never be a part of
our first-class mother's life.

496
00:33:09,958 --> 00:33:12,291
You can never replace
our dad in our lives.

497
00:33:12,375 --> 00:33:13,250
Never.

498
00:33:18,208 --> 00:33:20,125
Your dad's place is up there on the wall.

499
00:33:20,458 --> 00:33:21,791
I'd never want to take that place.

500
00:33:22,208 --> 00:33:23,916
I'll carve out my own place in this house.

501
00:33:24,500 --> 00:33:25,375
Juice.

502
00:33:25,750 --> 00:33:28,083
Do you want to make
your own place in this house?

503
00:33:29,416 --> 00:33:31,291
So, shall we start discussing
your marriage with Gangubai?

504
00:33:35,666 --> 00:33:36,541
Hey!

505
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:38,416
What am I going to do with this trash?

506
00:33:38,500 --> 00:33:40,708
- No way. Get lost.
- Gangu <i>ji…</i>

507
00:33:41,375 --> 00:33:42,750
what do you think about me?

508
00:33:43,875 --> 00:33:44,833
Hey, idiot!

509
00:33:45,541 --> 00:33:49,500
I rejected Ajay Devgn,
and you think I'd choose Sanjay Mishra?

510
00:33:49,916 --> 00:33:50,791
Get lost!

511
00:33:53,208 --> 00:33:55,000
Look, even she's not ready.

512
00:33:55,958 --> 00:33:56,958
Here come the snacks!

513
00:33:58,458 --> 00:33:59,333
Come, let's eat.

514
00:34:05,375 --> 00:34:07,125
- Excuse me, please.
- It's important.

515
00:34:09,083 --> 00:34:10,041
How's he?

516
00:34:17,250 --> 00:34:18,125
What?!

517
00:34:18,458 --> 00:34:19,916
Prithvi is coming
to Chamboli Ghat on Sunday?

518
00:34:20,250 --> 00:34:21,166
Is the information correct?

519
00:34:21,416 --> 00:34:22,291
Okay.

520
00:34:26,125 --> 00:34:27,041
Kids?

521
00:34:27,416 --> 00:34:30,541
Guddu, I think we need
to give some more time to the kids.

522
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:33,333
Let's go on a bonding trip this Sunday?

523
00:34:33,458 --> 00:34:34,458
