- Fine, who would lead the human chain?

1030
01:00:00,750 --> 01:00:01,625
Come forward!

1031
01:00:03,458 --> 01:00:04,791
Uncle, you're the bravest of all.

1032
01:00:05,458 --> 01:00:07,250
Me? Brave? How?

1033
01:00:07,625 --> 01:00:08,625
That's why you came forward.

1034
01:00:08,833 --> 01:00:09,708
No, I didn't.

1035
01:00:13,875 --> 01:00:15,833
I don't know how,
but every time there's danger,

1036
01:00:16,083 --> 01:00:18,083
I somehow end up stepping
forward first.

1037
01:00:18,375 --> 01:00:19,583
Adi!

1038
01:00:21,166 --> 01:00:23,416
Help! Please, hurry up.

1039
01:00:23,666 --> 01:00:24,708
But where are you?

1040
01:00:24,958 --> 01:00:25,833
Where are you?

1041
01:00:26,041 --> 01:00:27,041
Go ahead and check.

1042
01:00:32,625 --> 01:00:33,916
Don't let go of the hand.

1043
01:00:34,166 --> 01:00:35,875
Hold each other's hands.

1044
01:00:36,125 --> 01:00:37,625
Hold each other's hands tightly.

1045
01:00:38,208 --> 01:00:41,208
Listen, extend your hand.
Extend your hand.

1046
01:00:42,875 --> 01:00:44,125
Very good!

1047
01:00:44,208 --> 01:00:45,541
Come on. Keep holding my hands.

1048
01:00:46,083 --> 01:00:48,458
Please, do something.

1049
01:00:50,000 --> 01:00:52,000
Give your hand. Come on.

1050
01:00:52,291 --> 01:00:54,208
Okay… don't move now.

1051
01:00:55,750 --> 01:00:57,916
Don't worry.
I'm holding this tree.

1052
01:00:58,000 --> 01:01:01,333
The tree won't run away.
Hold me tightly.

1053
01:01:01,750 --> 01:01:02,625
Stand straight, all of you.

1054
01:01:03,125 --> 01:01:04,458
I will try to reach him.

1055
01:01:04,541 --> 01:01:05,958
Yes. Bro, concentrate.

1056
01:01:06,333 --> 01:01:07,833
Concentrate!

1057
01:01:07,916 --> 01:01:09,708
- Bro, concentrate.
- Bend, guys. Bend a little.

1058
01:01:09,875 --> 01:01:11,375
- Bend a little more.
- Concentrate!

1059
01:01:11,541 --> 01:01:12,500
- Bend more.
- Concentrate.

1060
01:01:12,750 --> 01:01:14,375
- Concentrate.
- Enough. We're bending too much.

1061
01:01:14,541 --> 01:01:15,458
Come on.

1062
01:01:15,833 --> 01:01:16,708
Come. Come.

1063
01:01:16,791 --> 01:01:18,375
Come on.

1064
01:01:18,458 --> 01:01:19,625
- Come on.
- Be careful!

1065
01:01:19,875 --> 01:01:21,166
Come down a little.

1066
01:01:24,416 --> 01:01:25,958
Why are they going in reverse?

1067
01:01:26,166 --> 01:01:28,208
Who's dragging everyone?

1068
01:01:28,958 --> 01:01:33,375
- Oh no!
- Guddu, please don't do that.

1069
01:01:34,958 --> 01:01:36,750
Very good!

1070
01:01:36,833 --> 01:01:38,125
Yes! Yes!

1071
01:01:38,208 --> 01:01:40,083
Yes, Guddu! Very good!

1072
01:01:40,875 --> 01:01:41,875
Very good, Guddu!

1073
01:01:41,958 --> 01:01:43,333
Be careful! Come!

1074
01:01:43,791 --> 01:01:45,625
- Come. Come.
- Come down a little. Come.

1075
01:01:45,833 --> 01:01:47,125
The cliff has become an escalator.

1076
01:01:51,000 --> 01:01:51,875
Oh no!

1077
01:01:52,500 --> 01:01:54,291
Hey, Guddu!

1078
01:01:54,583 --> 01:01:56,500
- Guddu!
- Prithvi.

1079
01:01:57,333 --> 01:01:58,375
- Guddu.
- Yes?

1080
01:01:58,583 --> 01:02:00,166
I'm losing my grip!

1081
01:02:02,291 --> 01:02:05,333
I'm going straight out in one shot!

1082
01:02:05,833 --> 01:02:08,416
Guddu, I'm gone.

1083
01:02:08,625 --> 01:02:10,458
Don't be scared! I'll pull you up.

1084
01:02:10,750 --> 01:02:12,041
- Wait!
- Guddu!

1085
01:02:12,875 --> 01:02:14,875
I betrayed you so many times,

1086
01:02:15,750 --> 01:02:18,500
yet every single time,
you saved me. But now…

1087
01:02:19,166 --> 01:02:20,083
I won't survive.

1088
01:02:20,791 --> 01:02:23,541
This is the punishment for my greed.

1089
01:02:23,750 --> 01:02:25,458
Hey, stop this emotional drama!

1090
01:02:25,625 --> 01:02:26,625
Tell us the secret of the treasure.

1091
01:02:27,166 --> 01:02:29,833
And tell him to say the location
of the treasure loudly.

1092
01:02:30,083 --> 01:02:32,583
- Otherwise, my hand will slip.
- Hey!

1093
01:02:32,666 --> 01:02:34,166
Speak louder! Louder! Come on.

1094
01:02:34,916 --> 01:02:40,541
Janakpur Jetty is 50 kilometers from here.

1095
01:02:41,625 --> 01:02:46,958
From there, 120 kilometers south
into the sea,

1096
01:02:47,625 --> 01:02:50,541
there's an island.

1097
01:02:50,625 --> 01:02:51,500
An island.

1098
01:02:52,000 --> 01:02:52,958
What's the name?

1099
01:02:53,041 --> 01:02:55,083
Prithvi Deshpande!

1100
01:02:55,375 --> 01:02:56,625
What do we do with your name?

1101
01:02:56,833 --> 01:02:57,708
Tell us the name of that island.

1102
01:02:57,958 --> 01:03:00,666
The island does not have any name.

1103
01:03:00,875 --> 01:03:02,500
How do I search on Google Maps?

1104
01:03:02,791 --> 01:03:04,500
Come on, it must have a name.

1105
01:03:05,083 --> 01:03:06,791
Do you want to make
an identity card for that island?

1106
01:03:07,833 --> 01:03:08,708
Please, continue.

1107
01:03:08,958 --> 01:03:12,708
You will easily identify that island.

1108
01:03:13,625 --> 01:03:18,541
There's a giant "M" on the island.
A giant "M".

1109
01:03:18,875 --> 01:03:20,791
- "M."
- "M" for mother?

1110
01:03:21,041 --> 01:03:21,916
Yes.

1111
01:03:22,458 --> 01:03:23,958
"M" for Mother.

1112
01:03:24,458 --> 01:03:27,000
Adi, I miss Mom.

1113
01:03:27,083 --> 01:03:28,625
This is not the time, Manav!

1114
01:03:29,250 --> 01:03:32,000
But how do we identify that giant "M"?

1115
01:03:32,708 --> 01:03:34,791
That giant "M" is made out of mountains.

1116
01:03:34,875 --> 01:03:37,250
You'll be able to spot it from far away.

1117
01:03:38,083 --> 01:03:41,000
But to reach that "M",

1118
01:03:41,500 --> 01:03:45,333
you'll have to pass through
a dense and dangerous jungle!

1119
01:03:45,583 --> 01:03:46,583
Tell us,

1120
01:03:46,833 --> 01:03:49,250
where will we find the treasure
once we reach that giant "M"?

1121
01:03:49,333 --> 01:03:50,708
Yes, please clarify that.

1122
01:03:50,958 --> 01:03:53,041
The treasure is beneath that giant "M",

1123
01:03:54,125 --> 01:03:57,291
behind an "O".

1124
01:03:57,458 --> 01:03:58,375
- Behind what?
- Behind an "O"?

1125
01:03:58,458 --> 01:04:00,750
Beneath the "M",

1126
01:04:01,583 --> 01:04:07,416
behind an "O".

1127
01:04:12,750 --> 01:04:14,458
- He's gone.
- Hey, Adi.

1128
01:04:14,541 --> 01:04:15,416
He's gone.

1129
01:04:15,541 --> 01:04:16,541
Adi, even he is gone.

1130
01:04:17,000 --> 01:04:19,250
- Who?
- The one who held my hand.

1131
01:04:21,333 --> 01:04:23,208
Hold him. Hold him.

1132
01:04:29,583 --> 01:04:31,125
- We are safe. We are safe.
- Guddu…

1133
01:04:31,500 --> 01:04:33,458
We are safe. We are safe.

1134
01:04:33,583 --> 01:04:36,916
It feels like death
itself is coming for us.

1135
01:04:37,041 --> 01:04:38,625
Hey, snail, crawl up.

1136
01:04:38,708 --> 01:04:40,875
Manav, pull up.

1137
01:04:41,166 --> 01:04:43,208
Adi, we will die.

1138
01:04:43,375 --> 01:04:46,250
Don't worry. Cheaters like us
don't die so easily.

1139
01:04:46,333 --> 01:04:47,708
Keep moving. Carefully.

1140
01:04:48,208 --> 01:04:49,333
Come on. Carefully.

1141
01:04:49,708 --> 01:04:51,916
- Come on. Come on, Manav.
- Yes. Come.

1142
01:04:54,291 --> 01:04:55,166
What was that?

1143
01:04:56,583 --> 01:04:57,458
What's happening?

1144
01:05:01,791 --> 01:05:03,708
- Adi…
- Come on, Manav.

1145
01:05:11,916 --> 01:05:13,375
Manav, crawl up fast.
Hurry up.

1146
01:05:13,458 --> 01:05:15,375
I am trying, Adi. I am trying.

1147
01:05:16,541 --> 01:05:17,500
Pull up, Manav.

1148
01:05:17,583 --> 01:05:19,708
- Crawl up, man.
- Hurry up.

1149
01:05:20,416 --> 01:05:22,000
Come on up.

1150
01:05:22,250 --> 01:05:24,166
Hurry up. Come on.

1151
01:05:25,333 --> 01:05:27,916
- Hurry up.
- Come on, Manav. Come on.

1152
01:05:28,041 --> 01:05:30,125
Come on. We're almost there.

1153
01:05:31,166 --> 01:05:32,083
Hey…

1154
01:05:33,250 --> 01:05:34,125
Sorry, bro.

1155
01:05:34,208 --> 01:05:36,541
- Sorry for what, bro?
- For this.

1156
01:05:38,041 --> 01:05:39,458
Hey, Uncle Johnny!

1157
01:05:41,583 --> 01:05:43,625
- He said sorry, then kicked me, bro!
- Adi!

1158
01:05:43,708 --> 01:05:44,791
- Uncle, this is cheating.
- Adi, let's go.

1159
01:05:44,875 --> 01:05:46,375
- This is cheating!
- I like to cheat! I like to cheat!

1160
01:05:46,458 --> 01:05:48,125
- Let's go, Manav.
- Uncle, this is cheating.

1161
01:05:48,291 --> 01:05:49,208
Johnny!

1162
01:05:49,583 --> 01:05:52,708
- Come on, Johnny. Crawl up.
- Try it to climb up.

1163
01:05:52,791 --> 01:05:54,375
- Yes, crawl up. Try.
- Yes, try to crawl up.

1164
01:05:54,458 --> 01:05:55,875
- Crawl.
- Yes, very good.

1165
01:05:56,291 --> 01:05:59,250
- Good! Very good!
- Don't give up. Very good.

1166
01:06:01,375 --> 01:06:03,208
- Careful!
- Be careful!

1167
01:06:03,458 --> 01:06:04,750
I got hold of the branch, bro!

1168
01:06:06,333 --> 01:06:07,375
- Come up.
- Come on.

1169
01:06:07,458 --> 01:06:08,500
I hope this tree won't get uprooted.

1170
01:06:08,583 --> 01:06:10,375
- Oh, no! Come with me!
- Oh, no!

1171
01:06:12,583 --> 01:06:14,375
Don't let go, Johnny! Hang on!

1172
01:06:15,958 --> 01:06:17,416
Bro, keep holding tight!

1173
01:06:25,666 --> 01:06:28,250
Wait. Hold on tight.

1174
01:06:28,458 --> 01:06:29,708
- Bro!
- Don't let go!

1175
01:06:29,875 --> 01:06:31,166
- Johnny!
- I won't!

1176
01:06:32,125 --> 01:06:34,125
Nala and Neela built the Ram Setu bridge.

1177
01:06:34,458 --> 01:06:37,041
- You make me your bridge. Bro.
- I'm coming.

1178
01:06:37,125 --> 01:06:38,583
- Hold on tight.
- Don't worry, bro.

1179
01:06:38,666 --> 01:06:40,250
No, I can't…

1180
01:06:41,416 --> 01:06:44,000
Wait, Johnny.
Don't let go, Johnny.

1181
01:06:44,250 --> 01:06:46,500
Johnny, don't let go.
Don't let go.

1182
01:06:48,416 --> 01:06:49,500
Pull me up, bro.

1183
01:06:50,458 --> 01:06:52,583
Hold on. Let me catch my breath.

1184
01:06:53,333 --> 01:06:54,666
Johnny, wait and see.

1185
01:06:55,166 --> 01:06:57,375
No one can take the treasure except me.

1186
01:06:57,458 --> 01:07:00,875
Shut up! I'll take the treasure!

1187
01:07:00,958 --> 01:07:04,291
Paro, hop in! Quick!
We'll fly to the treasure.

1188
01:07:05,333 --> 01:07:06,333
Yes, I'm coming.

1189
01:07:07,000 --> 01:07:07,958
Is it fine?

1190
01:07:12,333 --> 01:07:14,000
It's really windy, Paro.

1191
01:07:14,458 --> 01:07:15,958
Hey, my hot-air balloon!

1192
01:07:19,125 --> 01:07:20,125
My hot-air balloon!

1193
01:07:24,666 --> 01:07:25,916
My hot-air balloon!

1194
01:07:26,000 --> 01:07:28,541
Bye-bye!
We will return it to you soon!

1195
01:07:31,083 --> 01:07:32,083
My hot-air balloon!

1196
01:07:32,166 --> 01:07:35,041
Will you turn this bicycle into
an airplane to catch us?

1197
01:07:35,458 --> 01:07:37,458
Look in the front.
Look in the front.

1198
01:07:40,625 --> 01:07:41,750
See, you caused an accident.

1199
01:07:41,833 --> 01:07:44,458
Goodbye! Enjoy the fish fry!

1200
01:07:45,166 --> 01:07:46,041
Listen,

1201
01:07:46,875 --> 01:07:49,750
we shouldn't have
left them to die.

1202
01:07:49,833 --> 01:07:51,125
Nothing will happen to them.

1203
01:07:51,458 --> 01:07:53,375
All of them are cheaters.

1204
01:07:53,750 --> 01:07:55,208
They must have managed to crawl up
and must be chasing us.

1205
01:07:56,333 --> 01:07:57,708
{\an8}You weren't in <i>Total Dhamaal,</i> right?

1206
01:07:58,166 --> 01:07:59,041
{\an8}But I was there.

1207
01:07:59,750 --> 01:08:02,750
{\an8}Stop thinking about them.
Enjoy this scenery.

1208
01:08:04,250 --> 01:08:05,750
Hey, look there.

1209
01:08:07,833 --> 01:08:09,916
Such a beautiful Indra Kumar.

1210
01:08:10,875 --> 01:08:13,958
Well, it's "Indra Dhanush".

1211
01:08:14,416 --> 01:08:16,166
Whatever it is.

1212
01:08:16,541 --> 01:08:18,083
Both are exceptional.

1213
01:08:19,291 --> 01:08:20,583
Someday I will tell you their stories.

1214
01:08:21,750 --> 01:08:23,875
Listen to this story right away.
At the time of shooting…

1215
01:08:28,458 --> 01:08:32,166
My boat.

1216
01:08:32,250 --> 01:08:33,791
Adi, that fatso is running after us.

1217
01:08:33,875 --> 01:08:36,250
My boat.
I won't let you go.

1218
01:08:37,541 --> 01:08:38,458
Oh no!

1219
01:08:38,541 --> 01:08:39,666
He fell into the water.

1220
01:08:40,250 --> 01:08:41,750
I don't know him.
Leave it. Look in the front.

1221
01:08:41,833 --> 01:08:42,708
Okay.

1222
01:08:42,791 --> 01:08:45,166
Adi! That bearded beggar left us
and ran away.

1223
01:08:45,750 --> 01:08:47,250
Bloody basket! Cheater cock.

1224
01:08:47,500 --> 01:08:48,500
He was quite cunning.

1225
01:08:48,625 --> 01:08:50,541
If I find him, I won't spare him.

1226
01:08:50,625 --> 01:08:51,541
Yes, Adi.

1227
01:09:07,833 --> 01:09:08,833
Bro, what have you done?

1228
01:09:10,083 --> 01:09:11,791
Hey, my boat. My boat.

1229
01:09:12,916 --> 01:09:15,333
- Yeah…
- Bro.

1230
01:09:16,041 --> 01:09:18,458
Were these greedy idiots the only people
you could find to ask for help?

1231
01:09:18,833 --> 01:09:20,208
Those fellows ran away, leaving
us to die!

1232
01:09:20,291 --> 01:09:22,166
But they looked decent
and innocent to us!

1233
01:09:22,250 --> 01:09:24,458
How can you tell if someone
is decent just by his face?

1234
01:09:24,791 --> 01:09:25,666
Just look at bro!

1235
01:09:26,208 --> 01:09:27,750
- Hey, you…
- I am sorry.

1236
01:09:27,833 --> 01:09:29,250
- Control the boat.
- Bro…

1237
01:09:29,416 --> 01:09:30,416
Bro! Bro!

1238
01:09:32,000 --> 01:09:33,125
I won't spare those people.

1239
01:09:33,291 --> 01:09:34,541
Hey, first pick up some speed.

1240
01:09:34,625 --> 01:09:37,041
- Yeah, speed up, Guddu!
- Speed up.

1241
01:09:42,166 --> 01:09:45,791
Paro, you may have played
with the balloons in childhood.

1242
01:09:46,208 --> 01:09:47,208
But did you ever imagine

1243
01:09:47,375 --> 01:09:49,541
that one day you would fly
in a hot air balloon?

1244
01:09:50,625 --> 01:09:52,125
Never imagined it…

1245
01:09:52,416 --> 01:09:54,500
But this is so much fun!

1246
01:09:54,583 --> 01:09:56,166
When we find the treasure,

1247
01:09:56,583 --> 01:09:58,208
it'll be even more fun.

1248
01:10:09,166 --> 01:10:10,208
How much do you eat?

1249
01:10:10,625 --> 01:10:12,416
Your stomach is rumbling so loudly!

1250
01:10:14,625 --> 01:10:16,125
{\an8}My stomach isn't upset.

1251
01:10:17,291 --> 01:10:18,166
{\an8}Look over there.

1252
01:10:18,541 --> 01:10:19,791
{\an8}Your stomach will get upset.

1253
01:10:27,250 --> 01:10:28,375
Not just the stomach.

1254
01:10:28,791 --> 01:10:30,916
{\an8}Pants will get ruined, too.

1255
01:10:37,916 --> 01:10:39,833
Once we get our hands
on this treasure,

1256
01:10:39,958 --> 01:10:41,875
we'll become billionaires very soon!

1257
01:10:42,416 --> 01:10:44,500
According to that, how much
is my share, <i>bhabhi?</i>

1258
01:10:44,583 --> 01:10:46,541
Simple, Manav.
One share yours, one mine,

1259
01:10:46,625 --> 01:10:47,708
and one will be of your <i>bhabhi's.</i>

1260
01:10:48,000 --> 01:10:49,125
Not so simple.

1261
01:10:49,333 --> 01:10:51,125
There will only be two shares
of the treasure.

1262
01:10:51,291 --> 01:10:53,875
Okay? One share is ours,
and one share is ours.

1263
01:10:54,083 --> 01:10:55,083
One share for me,

1264
01:10:55,250 --> 01:10:56,833
and one share for you two together.

1265
01:10:57,000 --> 01:10:57,875
How does that make sense?!

1266
01:10:57,958 --> 01:10:59,083
Two of you are one unit, right?

1267
01:10:59,375 --> 01:11:01,541
Yeah, Adi! Actually, we've been
brothers since childhood. Right?

1268
01:11:01,625 --> 01:11:02,875
Get lost.
"Brothers"!

1269
01:11:08,291 --> 01:11:09,166
Look there.

1270
01:11:09,958 --> 01:11:10,833
Over there.

1271
01:11:15,166 --> 01:11:17,166
Oh no! Adi,

1272
01:11:17,333 --> 01:11:19,458
it seems the God of death
has found us again.

1273
01:11:19,625 --> 01:11:22,833
Mom, we are coming. Adi…

1274
01:11:29,291 --> 01:11:31,375
Guddu, if we find
Shaitaan Singh's treasure,

1275
01:11:31,458 --> 01:11:32,875
how rich will we become?

1276
01:11:33,125 --> 01:11:35,750
So rich that every Christmas,
you'll be giving gifts to Santa Claus!

1277
01:11:37,083 --> 01:11:38,458
I'm going to go shopping
every single day!

1278
01:11:38,583 --> 01:11:40,416
And what will you do,
Uncle Johnny?

1279
01:11:40,625 --> 01:11:43,375
Nothing. I'll find a nice match
and get married, bro.

1280
01:11:43,791 --> 01:11:44,666
Johnny dear,

1281
01:11:45,250 --> 01:11:47,708
at your age, not marriage proposals,
but angels come.

1282
01:11:48,041 --> 01:11:49,625
And that too, to take you
away with them.

1283
01:11:58,416 --> 01:12:02,625
Bro… who's going to save us
from this angel of death, bro?

1284
01:12:02,708 --> 01:12:03,708
What do we do, Uncle?

1285
01:12:18,791 --> 01:12:20,541
Help!

1286
01:12:21,458 --> 01:12:22,416
Mom!

1287
01:13:01,333 --> 01:13:02,416
What's happening?

1288
01:13:06,625 --> 01:13:07,625
Oh, God!

1289
01:13:08,208 --> 01:13:10,041
Please, save us this time.

1290
01:13:10,916 --> 01:13:12,458
I promise,

1291
01:13:13,291 --> 01:13:14,333
if we survive this storm,

1292
01:13:14,958 --> 01:13:18,625
I'll offer you 500 kilos of sweets.

1293
01:13:36,625 --> 01:13:40,416
- We survived! We survived!
- We survived.

1294
01:13:40,916 --> 01:13:44,458
Now, just remember to offer God
those sweets worth 150,000 rupees.

1295
01:13:45,625 --> 01:13:46,541
How 150,000?

1296
01:13:47,791 --> 01:13:49,125
You said 500 kilos.

1297
01:13:49,583 --> 01:13:50,708
At 300 rupees per kilo,

1298
01:13:50,791 --> 01:13:51,958
it will be 150,000 rupees'
worth of sweets, right?

1299
01:13:53,833 --> 01:13:55,291
You heard me wrong.

1300
01:13:55,583 --> 01:13:56,916
I didn't say 500 kilos,

1301
01:13:57,166 --> 01:14:00,125
I said 500 grams. 500 grams.

1302
01:14:03,625 --> 01:14:07,208
Why do you turn away
from your promise to God?

1303
01:14:07,291 --> 01:14:09,166
How do you know that?

1304
01:14:09,250 --> 01:14:11,208
I wasn't a part of <i>Total Dhamaal.</i>

1305
01:14:11,375 --> 01:14:12,833
But I had watched it.

1306
01:14:19,083 --> 01:14:21,666
Fire! There's a fire.

1307
01:14:22,125 --> 01:14:24,250
We're going to die.
We're going to die.

1308
01:14:24,375 --> 01:14:27,166
No! I won't let anything
happen to my husband.

1309
01:14:27,291 --> 01:14:28,875
You cannot die.

1310
01:14:31,375 --> 01:14:33,333
Hail Bajrangbali!

1311
01:14:35,500 --> 01:14:38,208
Oh, my husband!

1312
01:14:40,750 --> 01:14:42,916
Where are you going,
leaving me behind?

1313
01:14:43,416 --> 01:14:49,083
I'm leaving the whole world behind.

1314
01:14:51,458 --> 01:14:53,958
See you in the next life now.

1315
01:14:54,666 --> 01:14:58,666
Goodbye.

1316
01:15:05,208 --> 01:15:07,541
Thank God,
I have no motion sickness.

1317
01:15:07,625 --> 01:15:08,500
- Adi.
- Yes.

1318
01:15:08,583 --> 01:15:12,375
Looks like Lord Yamaraj
has sent his entire army after us.

1319
01:15:12,458 --> 01:15:13,958
- Yes, Manav.
- I told you

1320
01:15:14,291 --> 01:15:15,791
not to take a boat named <i>Titanic.</i>

1321
01:15:16,375 --> 01:15:18,166
It'll sink. We're all going to die.

1322
01:15:18,250 --> 01:15:20,208
None of you will die.

1323
01:15:20,416 --> 01:15:22,333
Because I will save everyone.

1324
01:15:23,666 --> 01:15:24,541
Oh no!

1325
01:15:26,416 --> 01:15:28,583
Octopus!

1326
01:15:35,083 --> 01:15:36,833
Manav, hit the octopus.

1327
01:15:37,458 --> 01:15:38,333
Hit it.

1328
01:15:38,791 --> 01:15:40,583
Break his legs.

1329
01:15:43,500 --> 01:15:44,833
Oh shit!

1330
01:15:47,250 --> 01:15:48,250
Where's the octopus?

1331
01:15:51,041 --> 01:15:52,208
Bloody basket!

1332
01:15:52,541 --> 01:15:54,750
Attacked my <i>bhabhi?</i>
I'll smash your head.

1333
01:15:55,208 --> 01:15:56,125
No… no… no…

1334
01:15:56,791 --> 01:15:57,666
Don't hit it.

1335
01:15:58,291 --> 01:15:59,208
Pull it off!

1336
01:15:59,291 --> 01:16:00,416
Okay, okay…

1337
01:16:00,500 --> 01:16:01,375
Leave.

1338
01:16:01,666 --> 01:16:03,333
Let go, you bald idiot.

1339
01:16:03,541 --> 01:16:05,958
I'll turn you into salad.

1340
01:16:08,916 --> 01:16:09,791
Come out.

1341
01:16:11,541 --> 01:16:13,666
Leave my <i>bhabhi </i>if you love your life.

1342
01:16:13,916 --> 01:16:16,041
Leave her. Let go.

1343
01:16:17,250 --> 01:16:18,208
I said let go.

1344
01:16:18,666 --> 01:16:20,833
Hey! Hey, what are you doing?!

1345
01:16:21,083 --> 01:16:22,333
I'm drowning it to death.

1346
01:16:23,125 --> 01:16:25,500
Who are you drowning to death?!

1347
01:16:25,791 --> 01:16:26,833
The octopus.

1348
01:16:30,708 --> 01:16:32,583
Idiot! Your <i>bhabhi </i>will die.

1349
01:16:32,833 --> 01:16:33,708
<i>Bhabhi </i>will die?

1350
01:16:33,791 --> 01:16:34,875
- Take her out.
- Oh shit!

1351
01:16:35,958 --> 01:16:36,833
What are you doing?

1352
01:16:36,916 --> 01:16:37,833
- You will kill your <i>bhabhi.</i>
- I am sorry, Adi.

1353
01:16:40,791 --> 01:16:44,041
Adi, this thing is attacking with
the whole family.

1354
01:16:47,041 --> 01:16:49,750
This storm doesn't seem to stop.

1355
01:16:50,583 --> 01:16:51,708
Don't panic!

1356
01:16:52,583 --> 01:16:54,041
This storm will stop soon.

1357
01:16:56,666 --> 01:16:58,000
What happened, bro?

1358
01:16:59,833 --> 01:17:01,375
The storm didn’t stop, but the boat did.

1359
01:17:01,833 --> 01:17:04,000
I'm not getting down to push it.

1360
01:17:04,083 --> 01:17:05,625
I’m a senior citizen, bro.

1361
01:17:05,708 --> 01:17:07,000
Hey, a while ago you were talking
about getting married.

1362
01:17:07,083 --> 01:17:08,041
Now, suddenly you became
a senior citizen?

1363
01:17:09,541 --> 01:17:11,375
Wait! I'll check.

1364
01:17:11,708 --> 01:17:13,708
- Yeah! Check.
- Hey, leave me first.

1365
01:17:19,458 --> 01:17:20,333
Check.

1366
01:17:20,416 --> 01:17:22,916
Concentrate, bro. Hold this.

1367
01:17:28,083 --> 01:17:29,583
- Start!
- Start!

1368
01:17:31,958 --> 01:17:33,125
- Guddu!
- Guddu! Bro.

1369
01:17:35,708 --> 01:17:36,625
Help me!

1370
01:17:36,875 --> 01:17:39,541
- Stop the boat! I'm drowning.
- Guddu! Do something, Uncle.

1371
01:17:40,000 --> 01:17:41,708
Hey, Johnny! Johnny, stop the boat.

1372
01:17:42,333 --> 01:17:44,250
Johnny! Johnny, stop the boat.

1373
01:17:44,541 --> 01:17:45,416
Okay.

1374
01:17:48,750 --> 01:17:51,041
Hey, what are you doing?!

1375
01:17:53,875 --> 01:17:55,041
Which button did you press?

1376
01:17:55,250 --> 01:17:56,250
The red one.

1377
01:17:56,333 --> 01:17:57,416
You weren't supposed to press that.

1378
01:17:57,625 --> 01:17:58,833
Oh shit!

1379
01:17:58,916 --> 01:18:00,791
I forgot <i>Dhamaal 1,</i> bro.

1380
01:18:02,416 --> 01:18:03,541
Phone! Phone!

1381
01:18:05,583 --> 01:18:07,791
Phone… Aala… Aala…

1382
01:18:07,875 --> 01:18:08,875
Aaliya! Aaliya! Aaliya!

1383
01:18:09,125 --> 01:18:10,291
Guddu, where are you?

1384
01:18:10,708 --> 01:18:11,750
What are these strong winds

1385
01:18:12,166 --> 01:18:14,041
and this storm-like noise?

1386
01:18:14,333 --> 01:18:16,916
Oh… we… we're watching a movie.

1387
01:18:17,166 --> 01:18:18,375
<i>"Life Trapped in a Storm."</i>

1388
01:18:18,708 --> 01:18:19,833
Oh, okay.

1389
01:18:20,125 --> 01:18:21,541
I hope everything is going smoothly.

1390
01:18:21,708 --> 01:18:23,125
As smooth as water.

1391
01:18:23,625 --> 01:18:25,250
Okay, please let me talk to the kids.

1392
01:18:25,333 --> 01:18:27,041
Yes, just hold on.

1393
01:18:27,208 --> 01:18:29,000
Hey, phone… Phone…

1394
01:18:33,291 --> 01:18:34,166
Hello, Mom.

1395
01:18:34,250 --> 01:18:36,375
Hello, dear. Are you
enjoying yourselves?

1396
01:18:36,666 --> 01:18:38,333
Yes, we're watching a very good movie.

1397
01:18:38,500 --> 01:18:39,916
Oh, very good!

1398
01:18:40,083 --> 01:18:42,916
<i>Bhabhi…</i> hang up now.
Otherwise, the hero will die.

1399
01:18:43,125 --> 01:18:45,708
I mean… the hero is dying.

1400
01:18:45,875 --> 01:18:48,041
Good night, <i>bhabhi.</i> Good night!

1401
01:18:48,500 --> 01:18:49,375
Hang up.

1402
01:18:51,833 --> 01:18:52,708
Uncle!

1403
01:18:54,041 --> 01:18:54,916
What happened?

1404
01:18:55,000 --> 01:18:56,333
Looks like the hero isn't dying.

1405
01:18:57,250 --> 01:18:58,291
He has actually died.

1406
01:18:59,375 --> 01:19:00,875
A shark pulled him away.

1407
01:19:05,416 --> 01:19:07,625
Oh shit, Guddu bro.

1408
01:19:07,708 --> 01:19:09,666
Even you left us stranded in the middle.

1409
01:19:10,541 --> 01:19:12,833
People leave property
behind after their death,

1410
01:19:13,916 --> 01:19:17,166
but you left this cheap
jacket behind, bro.

1411
01:19:17,750 --> 01:19:21,000
My fate itself is cheap.

1412
01:19:38,250 --> 01:19:39,250
Hey, what's that?

1413
01:19:44,375 --> 01:19:45,500
Guddu bro,

1414
01:19:46,166 --> 01:19:48,458
is it your whole body
or just your head?

1415
01:19:50,833 --> 01:19:53,583
Hey, Guddu is following us
like the Sarkata monster.

1416
01:20:06,083 --> 01:20:08,875
Wow, Guddu bro! Riding a dolphin.

1417
01:20:11,291 --> 01:20:14,375
Bro, people usually
aim for a fish's eye.

1418
01:20:14,708 --> 01:20:17,708
But you rode on the fish.

1419
01:20:29,083 --> 01:20:30,000
Watch out for the pole.

1420
01:20:31,416 --> 01:20:32,333
Fool!

1421
01:20:33,958 --> 01:20:34,875
And the thorns!

1422
01:21:06,041 --> 01:21:06,958
Paro!

1423
01:21:07,458 --> 01:21:08,333
Open your eyes.

1424
01:21:18,291 --> 01:21:19,166
Hey!

1425
01:21:19,750 --> 01:21:21,125
Hey, look there.

1426
01:21:21,875 --> 01:21:23,416
I can see a giant "W".

1427
01:21:27,666 --> 01:21:28,583
"W?!"

1428
01:21:29,166 --> 01:21:31,791
We've gone so far in reverse that
we've reached the first <i>Dhamaal </i>again.

1429
01:21:32,541 --> 01:21:35,041
Good, at least we'll get ten crores.

1430
01:21:53,458 --> 01:21:56,125
Hey… this "W" is upside down.

1431
01:22:00,291 --> 01:22:01,541
This is an "M".

1432
01:22:02,458 --> 01:22:03,333
"M"!

1433
01:22:04,083 --> 01:22:05,875
We'll have to do something.
Knife?

1434
01:22:14,083 --> 01:22:15,000
Quickly, get up, Paro.

1435
01:22:15,375 --> 01:22:16,333
Get up! Come on.

1436
01:22:17,583 --> 01:22:18,458
Get up!

1437
01:22:20,000 --> 01:22:20,875
Look there.

1438
01:22:21,458 --> 01:22:22,500
Look there, Paro.

1439
01:22:23,500 --> 01:22:25,125
It's a giant "M".

1440
01:22:36,958 --> 01:22:39,625
Come on, Guddu, how many more thorns
are you going to get removed?

1441
01:22:39,708 --> 01:22:41,041
Yes, let's go, Guddu.

1442
01:22:41,541 --> 01:22:43,166
Have you pulled out all the thorns?

1443
01:22:43,958 --> 01:22:44,833
Bro.

1444
01:22:44,958 --> 01:22:46,125
Just sit in the water once.

1445
01:22:46,875 --> 01:22:48,375
Let me check all the punctures.

1446
01:22:49,166 --> 01:22:50,416
- Yeah.
- Shameless.

1447
01:22:52,125 --> 01:22:54,000
Bro is in this condition
because of you two.

1448
01:22:54,666 --> 01:22:55,958
You've come here for the treasure.

1449
01:22:56,208 --> 01:22:59,166
Yes, because we want
a lot of money for our mom.

1450
01:22:59,291 --> 01:23:01,250
I would have brought
the treasure for your mom.

1451
01:23:01,333 --> 01:23:02,791
Yes, but then you too
would have come along.

1452
01:23:02,916 --> 01:23:03,875
We don't want you.

1453
01:23:13,541 --> 01:23:14,875
Found it. Found it.

1454
01:23:14,958 --> 01:23:16,458
- What did you find now?
- What did you find?

1455
01:23:19,333 --> 01:23:20,250
"M".

1456
01:23:23,500 --> 01:23:25,208
- "M". Let's go. Come on.
- Damn!

1457
01:23:25,291 --> 01:23:26,333
Come on. Let's go.

1458
01:23:27,041 --> 01:23:28,625
Adi! Adi!

1459
01:23:28,833 --> 01:23:29,875
Adi, <i>bhabhi…</i>

1460
01:23:30,166 --> 01:23:31,166
<i>Bhabhi…</i>

1461
01:23:31,416 --> 01:23:33,416
Adi! Adi!

1462
01:23:33,750 --> 01:23:34,666
Adi!

1463
01:23:35,041 --> 01:23:36,000
- Adi!
- What happened?

1464
01:23:36,125 --> 01:23:37,000
Adi, <i>Bhabhi…</i>

1465
01:23:37,083 --> 01:23:38,291
Adi, <i>Bhabhi…</i>

1466
01:23:38,708 --> 01:23:39,625
Half <i>bhabhi?</i>

1467
01:23:40,125 --> 01:23:41,458
Where's the other half of <i>bhabhi?</i>

1468
01:23:41,541 --> 01:23:43,166
<i>Bhabhi </i>has left us.

1469
01:23:43,250 --> 01:23:45,000
- What did you do, Manav?
- Adi, please…

1470
01:23:45,083 --> 01:23:48,125
What did you do this time
that she ran away again?

1471
01:23:48,333 --> 01:23:49,666
Adi, I didn't do anything.

1472
01:23:49,750 --> 01:23:50,958
It's God's doing.

1473
01:23:51,250 --> 01:23:52,916
Today, you've
actually become a widower.

1474
01:23:53,125 --> 01:23:54,000
Look there.

1475
01:23:56,833 --> 01:23:57,958
Hey, Rosy!

1476
01:23:59,208 --> 01:24:00,458
- Rosy!
<i>- Bhabhi!</i>

1477
01:24:00,541 --> 01:24:02,250
Rosy, why did you leave me alone?

1478
01:24:02,666 --> 01:24:04,125
I love you, Rosy.

1479
01:24:04,375 --> 01:24:06,958
How will I live without you?

1480
01:24:08,916 --> 01:24:09,791
Aren't you dead?

1481
01:24:10,958 --> 01:24:12,250
Do you want me to die?

1482
01:24:12,500 --> 01:24:14,833
- No! No. I don't want that.
- How can you even think about that?

1483
01:24:14,916 --> 01:24:17,000
I won't spare you easily.

1484
01:24:17,250 --> 01:24:19,333
What do you think you are?

1485
01:24:19,958 --> 01:24:22,500
- I don't need your "sorry."
- Oh, shit!

1486
01:24:22,666 --> 01:24:25,458
- I will hit you. You deserve that.
- Adi.

1487
01:24:25,583 --> 01:24:27,250
Adi… <i>Bhabhi…</i>

1488
01:24:27,375 --> 01:24:28,833
- I won't spare you.
- Adi! <i>Bhabhi…</i>

1489
01:24:29,125 --> 01:24:30,708
Shut up!

1490
01:24:39,000 --> 01:24:39,875
- "M".
- "M".

1491
01:24:39,958 --> 01:24:42,333
- 'M'.
- Yes.

1492
01:24:42,416 --> 01:24:43,708
- "M".
- Let's go.

1493
01:25:13,416 --> 01:25:14,291
Stop.

1494
01:25:18,125 --> 01:25:19,666
{\an8}Let us go, man.

1495
01:25:20,375 --> 01:25:21,958
{\an8}We came here by mistake.

1496
01:25:22,291 --> 01:25:23,875
{\an8}Please, spare us.

1497
01:25:26,333 --> 01:25:27,208
No… No… No…

1498
01:25:27,291 --> 01:25:29,666
- No… No… No… please.
- No… No…

1499
01:25:32,208 --> 01:25:33,125
We are safe.

1500
01:25:33,791 --> 01:25:34,666
We are safe.

1501
01:25:34,750 --> 01:25:36,666
Thank you very much
for sparing our lives.

1502
01:25:37,000 --> 01:25:39,041
Bless me, Uncle. Bye.
Let's go.

1503
01:25:39,125 --> 01:25:40,000
Stop.

1504
01:25:41,125 --> 01:25:42,416
What's it now?

1505
01:25:42,625 --> 01:25:43,666
Do not go.

1506
01:25:44,666 --> 01:25:45,666
My man…

1507
01:25:46,375 --> 01:25:47,375
you fight…

1508
01:25:47,750 --> 01:25:48,666
What is he saying?

1509
01:25:48,791 --> 01:25:49,833
If you remain alive…

1510
01:25:50,708 --> 01:25:51,750
you can go…

1511
01:25:51,833 --> 01:25:53,708
Are you a human or a pirated CD?

1512
01:25:53,916 --> 01:25:55,041
Getting stuck on every dialogue.

1513
01:25:55,333 --> 01:25:58,041
I think he's telling you

1514
01:25:58,583 --> 01:26:00,750
to fight with his man.

1515
01:26:00,833 --> 01:26:02,625
And if you win, we can go.

1516
01:26:05,583 --> 01:26:06,583
Who should I fight with?

1517
01:26:11,458 --> 01:26:12,583
Who's this Hu Ha?

1518
01:26:13,416 --> 01:26:14,291
Hu Ha, who?

1519
01:26:14,375 --> 01:26:15,416
Who is Hu Ha?

1520
01:26:25,083 --> 01:26:28,250
Paro, you take the treasure and enjoy.

1521
01:26:29,291 --> 01:26:31,333
I'm about to get finished here.

1522
01:26:37,416 --> 01:26:38,625
Chiku, you…

1523
01:26:39,625 --> 01:26:41,958
Both of you, fight.

1524
01:26:43,208 --> 01:26:44,125
- Chiku?
- Chiku?

1525
01:27:10,625 --> 01:27:12,708
Is he already standing
or yet to stand up?

1526
01:27:16,666 --> 01:27:18,250
Will this short fellow fight with me?

1527
01:27:22,000 --> 01:27:24,583
You look more like a grape
than a <i>chiku!</i>

1528
01:27:28,208 --> 01:27:31,625
You can't even pluck
a mango from a tree.

1529
01:27:31,708 --> 01:27:33,416
Will you break my bones?

1530
01:27:35,250 --> 01:27:38,833
Hey, Paro, now we will take
the treasure and go together.

1531
01:27:39,500 --> 01:27:43,000
I will deal with him right away.

1532
01:27:43,458 --> 01:27:44,791
Go… Go…

1533
01:27:59,166 --> 01:28:00,916
Why do you bite like a dog?

1534
01:28:05,250 --> 01:28:08,000
Leave me.

1535
01:28:15,166 --> 01:28:16,458
What are you doing?

1536
01:28:41,750 --> 01:28:43,083
One moment.

1537
01:28:44,291 --> 01:28:46,000
Look up. Your mother.

1538
01:28:56,250 --> 01:28:57,166
Paro!

1539
01:28:57,416 --> 01:28:59,541
You're thinking about
seven lifetimes together…

1540
01:28:59,666 --> 01:29:04,333
This guy is going to kill me
for fourteen lifetimes, man!

1541
01:29:10,875 --> 01:29:13,166
I will never have kids.

1542
01:29:14,333 --> 01:29:16,125
You better remarry. Paro.

1543
01:29:19,333 --> 01:29:24,750
Where did that destroyer
of my family line go?

1544
01:29:31,750 --> 01:29:33,916
I'll send him to his maker!

1545
01:29:34,500 --> 01:29:37,166
Paro, give me a spear.

1546
01:29:37,250 --> 01:29:38,541
- Quickly!
- Spear…

1547
01:29:39,125 --> 01:29:40,000
Found it.

1548
01:29:40,500 --> 01:29:41,458
Come on, give it to me.

1549
01:29:49,041 --> 01:29:50,333
What kind of a woman are you?

1550
01:29:50,833 --> 01:29:53,416
You're practically
making yourself a widow.

1551
01:29:55,291 --> 01:29:57,208
Not even one of my legs is left intact.

1552
01:30:06,458 --> 01:30:07,375
Chiku!

1553
01:30:13,583 --> 01:30:14,791
No… No… No…

1554
01:30:25,458 --> 01:30:26,375
Paro…

1555
01:30:28,291 --> 01:30:29,458
Chiku!

1556
01:30:39,333 --> 01:30:40,208
Chiku!

1557
01:30:45,333 --> 01:30:46,208
Chiku!

1558
01:30:46,333 --> 01:30:47,250
Chiku!

1559
01:30:54,166 --> 01:30:55,041
Paro?!

1560
01:30:55,625 --> 01:30:56,875
Attention everyone.

1561
01:30:57,291 --> 01:30:58,958
If you beat up my husband…

1562
01:30:59,916 --> 01:31:01,375
your clan will be blown away.

1563
01:31:02,541 --> 01:31:03,500
None of you

1564
01:31:04,000 --> 01:31:05,083
will stay alive.

1565
01:31:05,833 --> 01:31:06,750
Understood?

1566
01:31:08,000 --> 01:31:10,041
We apologize!
We apologize!

1567
01:31:10,250 --> 01:31:11,208
We apologize!

1568
01:31:13,875 --> 01:31:16,041
No. No apology.

1569
01:31:16,750 --> 01:31:17,666
If my husband forgives you all,

1570
01:31:20,291 --> 01:31:21,291
only then will I forgive you.

1571
01:31:24,000 --> 01:31:25,250
We apologize.

1572
01:31:25,958 --> 01:31:27,583
We apologize.

1573
01:31:28,166 --> 01:31:30,458
- We apologize.
- Leave my legs, please.

1574
01:31:30,833 --> 01:31:32,666
It's already wounded.

1575
01:31:35,833 --> 01:31:36,791
Let's look ahead.

1576
01:31:42,458 --> 01:31:43,583
Why did you all stop?

1577
01:31:54,291 --> 01:31:55,333
He's asking something.
Tell him.

1578
01:31:55,791 --> 01:31:56,708
We are scared.

1579
01:31:57,250 --> 01:31:58,916
What if any wild animal appears?

1580
01:31:59,166 --> 01:32:01,166
Your general knowledge is very weak.

1581
01:32:01,333 --> 01:32:02,791
Wild animals don't live on the islands.

1582
01:32:02,958 --> 01:32:03,833
Hey, who is it?

1583
01:32:05,916 --> 01:32:06,833
They do.

1584
01:32:07,041 --> 01:32:08,250
- They do.
- Yes, they do.

1585
01:32:08,333 --> 01:32:10,500
This tiger's general
knowledge is very weak as well.

1586
01:32:10,708 --> 01:32:12,166
It came on an island. Idiot!

1587
01:32:18,291 --> 01:32:19,166
Oh God!

1588
01:32:19,250 --> 01:32:20,541
Singham on top
of another Singham!

1589
01:32:22,166 --> 01:32:24,000
Don't get into a scuffle with it.

1590
01:32:24,291 --> 01:32:25,291
Just run away.

1591
01:32:32,166 --> 01:32:33,541
No… No…

1592
01:32:35,625 --> 01:32:38,208
Hey, tiger… tiger…

1593
01:32:39,708 --> 01:32:40,750
What will you get by hunting me?

1594
01:32:42,166 --> 01:32:43,500
There are three more
items on the menu card.

1595
01:32:43,583 --> 01:32:45,875
- No.
- The smaller one is very tasty.

1596
01:32:46,333 --> 01:32:47,291
Aarav Do Pyaza.

1597
01:32:49,000 --> 01:32:49,875
Hey!

1598
01:32:50,083 --> 01:32:51,416
Hey, Guddu, have you lost it?

1599
01:32:52,958 --> 01:32:54,291
Don't panic.

1600
01:32:56,333 --> 01:32:57,708
I've read somewhere.

1601
01:32:59,000 --> 01:33:00,125
If you keep looking into a tiger's eye,

1602
01:33:01,125 --> 01:33:02,250
it won't attack.

1603
01:33:02,541 --> 01:33:04,000
Come on, tiger, look. Look here.

1604
01:33:05,416 --> 01:33:06,291
Watch!

1605
01:33:08,041 --> 01:33:08,916
Watch!

1606
01:33:11,958 --> 01:33:13,125
Yes… see.

1607
01:33:13,541 --> 01:33:14,541
It turned completely docile now.

1608
01:33:15,041 --> 01:33:16,500
- Wow!
- Told you my knowledge

1609
01:33:16,583 --> 01:33:17,583
about tigers is spot on.

1610
01:33:21,958 --> 01:33:22,833
What are you doing?

1611
01:33:23,000 --> 01:33:25,958
Bro, this tiger's general
knowledge is absolutely terrible.

1612
01:33:26,291 --> 01:33:28,041
It doesn't even know what it really is.

1613
01:33:29,708 --> 01:33:31,541
That tiger is going
to give him a disgraceful death!

1614
01:33:34,458 --> 01:33:35,333
Bro!

1615
01:33:46,875 --> 01:33:47,791
Saw what I did?

1616
01:33:54,291 --> 01:33:56,750
I've hit that idiot so hard,
it'll never come back again.

1617
01:34:12,375 --> 01:34:13,458
Hey, why are you screaming?

1618
01:34:14,666 --> 01:34:15,625
The tiger's gone now, right?

1619
01:34:16,083 --> 01:34:16,958
Let's go.

1620
01:34:18,916 --> 01:34:20,250
- Come on.
- Let's go.

1621
01:34:20,666 --> 01:34:22,416
- Bro is a genius.
- Yeah.

1622
01:34:32,208 --> 01:34:33,833
Adi, lizard…

1623
01:34:34,791 --> 01:34:35,708
Lizard…

1624
01:34:37,583 --> 01:34:38,500
You also must be tired.

1625
01:34:38,791 --> 01:34:39,666
Go drink some water.

1626
01:34:42,666 --> 01:34:43,625
I'm very thirsty.

1627
01:34:44,041 --> 01:34:45,166
Let me fill the bottle.

1628
01:34:45,250 --> 01:34:46,125
Okay.

1629
01:34:56,083 --> 01:34:59,708
Adi, you did a good thing
by giving water to the lizard.

1630
01:34:59,791 --> 01:35:01,291
Mom will be so proud of you.

1631
01:35:01,708 --> 01:35:02,916
- What?
- Yeah. Look there.

1632
01:35:03,000 --> 01:35:05,083
It was so thin and small.
After drinking water, it became so huge.

1633
01:35:05,833 --> 01:35:07,291
That's not a lizard.
That's your <i>bhabhi.</i>

1634
01:35:08,583 --> 01:35:10,333
Not her. The one next to her.

1635
01:35:10,416 --> 01:35:11,291
Take a look.

1636
01:35:13,833 --> 01:35:14,750
Oh shit!

1637
01:35:16,541 --> 01:35:18,833
Idiot, that's not a lizard.
That's a crocodile! A crocodile.

1638
01:35:21,541 --> 01:35:22,625
Stay quiet.

1639
01:35:26,583 --> 01:35:29,375
Adi, that small stone
can't kill the crocodile.

1640
01:35:30,375 --> 01:35:32,208
This is for your <i>bhabhi,</i> you idiot.

1641
01:35:32,500 --> 01:35:33,416
Okay.

1642
01:35:34,541 --> 01:35:36,083
What happened?
Why are you throwing stones?

1643
01:35:39,166 --> 01:35:40,041
What?

1644
01:35:40,750 --> 01:35:41,750
What is it?

1645
01:35:52,541 --> 01:35:53,416
Stay quiet.

1646
01:35:54,875 --> 01:35:57,708
Quietly walk backward. Slowly.

1647
01:35:58,000 --> 01:36:00,833
Come back slowly. Slowly.

1648
01:36:01,291 --> 01:36:04,041
Absolute silence.
Don't make a sound.

1649
01:36:11,583 --> 01:36:12,541
Adi, help!

1650
01:36:13,541 --> 01:36:14,541
Adi, help!

1651
01:36:14,625 --> 01:36:16,000
Adi, what do I do?

1652
01:36:16,083 --> 01:36:19,000
Poke in its eye!
Hurry up, poke in its eye!

1653
01:36:19,083 --> 01:36:20,541
- Okay… okay…
- Do it.

1654
01:36:20,791 --> 01:36:23,458
You idiot, poke the crocodile's eye.

1655
01:36:23,541 --> 01:36:24,666
Okay… okay…

1656
01:36:27,708 --> 01:36:28,666
Hey, statue!

1657
01:36:29,958 --> 01:36:30,958
Adi, it's not staying still.

1658
01:36:31,041 --> 01:36:33,166
You've got a knife, right? Cut it!

1659
01:36:33,291 --> 01:36:35,166
Cut it, come on.

1660
01:36:35,500 --> 01:36:36,375
Yes.

1661
01:36:37,416 --> 01:36:38,291
Adi!

1662
01:36:38,375 --> 01:36:40,541
This won't be enough
to cut the crocodile.

1663
01:36:40,750 --> 01:36:43,375
Idiot. Cut the bottle strap.
Come on.

1664
01:36:43,458 --> 01:36:45,083
Come on.
Yes, come on.

1665
01:36:45,166 --> 01:36:46,041
Come on, Manav.

1666
01:36:46,166 --> 01:36:47,041
Yes.

1667
01:36:48,166 --> 01:36:49,125
Oh my!

1668
01:36:49,625 --> 01:36:51,291
Adi… Adi…

1669
01:36:52,750 --> 01:36:53,833
Adi…

1670
01:36:57,708 --> 01:36:59,291
Run, run, run!

1671
01:37:11,041 --> 01:37:12,000
"M" is here.

1672
01:37:12,250 --> 01:37:13,875
We've reached near "M".

1673
01:37:14,458 --> 01:37:15,791
- Let's go.
- Come.

1674
01:37:22,083 --> 01:37:23,000
Get down!

1675
01:37:23,750 --> 01:37:24,625
Get down!

1676
01:37:29,458 --> 01:37:30,333
Get up.

1677
01:37:31,875 --> 01:37:33,958
Guddu, there could be danger inside.

1678
01:37:34,500 --> 01:37:36,333
There’s no danger,
there's only treasure inside.

1679
01:37:36,833 --> 01:37:38,625
Come on, hold each other's hands
and let's go.

1680
01:37:46,458 --> 01:37:48,708
"M". M for money.

1681
01:37:49,791 --> 01:37:50,916
M for…

1682
01:37:52,708 --> 01:37:54,458
Look there. The way to go inside.

1683
01:37:54,666 --> 01:37:55,541
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

1684
01:37:55,625 --> 01:37:56,833
Adi, there could be danger inside.

1685
01:37:56,916 --> 01:37:58,041
Just shut up.

1686
01:37:58,291 --> 01:37:59,208
Okay.

1687
01:38:03,041 --> 01:38:06,291
Paro, look there.

1688
01:38:07,416 --> 01:38:08,333
"M" is here.

1689
01:38:08,625 --> 01:38:09,500
Yeah!

1690
01:38:09,750 --> 01:38:10,625
Hey.

1691
01:38:12,458 --> 01:38:13,458
Look there.

1692
01:38:16,000 --> 01:38:20,625
Let's go inside and find
a way to enter "O".

1693
01:38:30,666 --> 01:38:33,666
Don't you find this place dangerous?

1694
01:38:35,791 --> 01:38:37,500
What's there to be scared of?

1695
01:38:37,708 --> 01:38:40,041
Just don't be scared.
Walk closely.

1696
01:38:40,333 --> 01:38:41,208
Keep walking.

1697
01:38:43,500 --> 01:38:47,208
Adi, this place looks
extremely dangerous.

1698
01:38:48,166 --> 01:38:49,625
You think you'll find
Shaitaan Singh's treasure

1699
01:38:49,708 --> 01:38:50,666
in a coffee shop?

1700
01:38:52,291 --> 01:38:53,166
Found it.

1701
01:38:57,166 --> 01:38:58,625
This must be the way
to get into the "O".

1702
01:38:59,000 --> 01:39:00,125
- Yes! Yes!
- Come on. Let's go.

1703
01:39:00,958 --> 01:39:01,833
Pull it, <i>bhabhi.</i>

1704
01:39:13,708 --> 01:39:15,250
It's really quiet here.

1705
01:39:23,291 --> 01:39:25,458
{\an8}Listen, Paro. Don't flirt.

1706
01:39:26,041 --> 01:39:27,333
I only let you hold my finger,

1707
01:39:27,416 --> 01:39:29,291
and you've already got your whole hand
inside my shirt!

1708
01:39:29,791 --> 01:39:31,208
{\an8}Is this really the time to get romantic?

1709
01:39:31,541 --> 01:39:33,208
{\an8}I didn't do anything.

1710
01:39:33,291 --> 01:39:35,500
{\an8}Really? You didn't do anything?

1711
01:39:35,916 --> 01:39:36,875
{\an8}You didn't do anything, huh?

1712
01:39:37,541 --> 01:39:38,416
Then…

1713
01:39:39,416 --> 01:39:40,291
what is this?

1714
01:39:40,583 --> 01:39:42,666
What is this? Tell me!

1715
01:39:44,458 --> 01:39:46,041
You got scared looking at your own hand?

1716
01:39:46,541 --> 01:39:49,208
That's not my hand. It's a snake!

1717
01:39:50,958 --> 01:39:51,958
It's a snake?

1718
01:39:52,416 --> 01:39:53,291
It's a…

1719
01:39:55,333 --> 01:39:56,541
It really is a snake.

1720
01:39:59,333 --> 01:40:01,125
Why is it flicking its tongue so much?

1721
01:40:02,458 --> 01:40:04,791
He turned out to be a Casanova
among snakes.

1722
01:40:05,375 --> 01:40:08,000
Listen, buddy, this is a family film.

1723
01:40:08,333 --> 01:40:10,791
That stuff doesn't happen here.

1724
01:40:12,833 --> 01:40:15,625
- Run! Run! Run!
- Run!

1725
01:40:19,083 --> 01:40:19,958
Bro.

1726
01:40:21,250 --> 01:40:22,166
Bro, stop.

1727
01:40:22,833 --> 01:40:24,458
- It's too dark.
- I'm scared.

1728
01:40:24,541 --> 01:40:27,375
My eyes have night vision.
I can see everything.

1729
01:40:37,083 --> 01:40:38,000
We survived.

1730
01:40:38,083 --> 01:40:38,958
We survived.

1731
01:40:39,541 --> 01:40:40,458
We survived.

1732
01:40:42,166 --> 01:40:43,041
Adi!

1733
01:40:43,125 --> 01:40:44,833
- What happened?
- We won't survive!

1734
01:41:07,625 --> 01:41:08,666
No… no… Don't move.

1735
01:41:09,083 --> 01:41:10,625
Don't move. Don't move.

1736
01:41:12,708 --> 01:41:13,833
Don't sneeze. No.

1737
01:41:13,958 --> 01:41:15,000
Don't sneeze. Please, no.

1738
01:41:15,333 --> 01:41:16,208
Don't sneeze.

1739
01:41:16,333 --> 01:41:17,250
Thank you.

1740
01:41:17,333 --> 01:41:18,208
Thank you.

1741
01:41:39,125 --> 01:41:41,583
Bro, we survived this time as well.

1742
01:41:55,958 --> 01:41:56,958
You too have reached?

1743
01:41:57,750 --> 01:41:59,833
Bro, he was the one who kicked.

1744
01:41:59,916 --> 01:42:00,833
Damn, you…

1745
01:42:05,916 --> 01:42:07,083
Oh shit!

1746
01:42:07,166 --> 01:42:08,875
Help! Help!

1747
01:42:08,958 --> 01:42:09,916
He has been crushed.

1748
01:42:10,083 --> 01:42:12,125
- Help!
- I am here.

1749
01:42:12,375 --> 01:42:14,625
Because you're here,
I need help. Get up, now.

1750
01:42:14,708 --> 01:42:15,791
Yes, yes.

1751
01:42:19,416 --> 01:42:20,666
So, you people made it here, too?

1752
01:42:21,208 --> 01:42:22,333
Even this traitor showed up.

1753
01:42:22,625 --> 01:42:23,541
Beat him up.

1754
01:42:23,833 --> 01:42:26,125
- Beat him up.
- Hey…

1755
01:42:28,166 --> 01:42:30,416
Don't you dare touch my husband!

1756
01:42:30,833 --> 01:42:32,500
I will crush him right here.

1757
01:42:32,833 --> 01:42:35,208
Madam, you don't know us.

1758
01:42:35,458 --> 01:42:37,375
We are the dangerous villains.

1759
01:42:37,458 --> 01:42:38,375
Right, Bro?

1760
01:42:38,625 --> 01:42:40,208
You look more like a comedian.

1761
01:42:41,458 --> 01:42:42,916
With one tight slap,
you will start saying,

1762
01:42:43,000 --> 01:42:45,208
"Sister, I've never
seen someone like you."

1763
01:42:45,333 --> 01:42:48,000
Listen, we don't raise our
hands on women. Understand?

1764
01:42:48,083 --> 01:42:49,416
But I do raise my hand on men.

1765
01:42:50,541 --> 01:42:51,625
Come on. Come forward.

1766
01:42:51,750 --> 01:42:54,083
Adi, woman power.
Don't mess.

1767
01:42:54,333 --> 01:42:56,875
Stop fighting and look for the "O".

1768
01:42:57,041 --> 01:42:58,708
Good idea. Let's look
for the "O". Where's it?

1769
01:42:59,000 --> 01:43:01,416
- "O".
- Yes, Bro, "O".

1770
01:43:01,625 --> 01:43:03,708
- Find the "O".
- Where's the "O"?

1771
01:43:03,791 --> 01:43:05,208
- Where's "O"?
- Look there.

1772
01:43:05,666 --> 01:43:06,541
Where?

1773
01:43:08,000 --> 01:43:09,000
{\an8}Those are the skeletons.

1774
01:43:09,125 --> 01:43:10,791
Does that mean people were
trapped and have died even here?

1775
01:43:12,000 --> 01:43:14,083
That means we will also die
and get trapped here, Adi.

1776
01:43:14,166 --> 01:43:15,500
Guddu! We don't want to die.
Please, save us.

1777
01:43:15,583 --> 01:43:17,833
- Save me this time, Bro.
- Leave me.

1778
01:43:18,875 --> 01:43:19,750
Wait!

1779
01:43:21,041 --> 01:43:21,958
Seems so.

1780
01:43:23,500 --> 01:43:25,416
There's no way out of this place.

1781
01:43:27,166 --> 01:43:28,666
Damn, this Shaitan Singh!

1782
01:43:30,333 --> 01:43:31,208
Guddu!

1783
01:43:32,250 --> 01:43:33,625
Is your hand hollow?

1784
01:43:33,708 --> 01:43:34,833
It’s sounding hollow.

1785
01:43:35,125 --> 01:43:36,583
Idiot, this wall is hollow.

1786
01:43:37,458 --> 01:43:39,333
If the wall is hollow,
let's break it.

1787
01:43:40,291 --> 01:43:41,208
Stone! Stone!

1788
01:43:41,291 --> 01:43:43,541
Yes, pick up the stone.

1789
01:43:43,625 --> 01:43:45,750
Let's break it with stones.

1790
01:44:09,541 --> 01:44:10,416
Bro!

1791
01:44:11,875 --> 01:44:13,291
The treasure, Bro!

1792
01:44:13,958 --> 01:44:14,916
Oh, damn!

1793
01:44:18,291 --> 01:44:19,291
The treasure!

1794
01:44:19,416 --> 01:44:21,083
- Let's get it, bro.
- Treasure.

1795
01:44:36,375 --> 01:44:37,708
We found the treasure!

1796
01:44:37,791 --> 01:44:38,833
Let's go. Let's go.

1797
01:44:38,916 --> 01:44:42,416
- The treasure.
- Come on. Manav, let's grab it.

1798
01:44:42,500 --> 01:44:43,375
Come on. Come on.

1799
01:44:43,625 --> 01:44:45,416
- Treasure.
- Here. Here.

1800
01:44:45,875 --> 01:44:47,916
So much money!
So much treasure!

1801
01:44:49,375 --> 01:44:50,875
Let me grab it.

1802
01:44:51,500 --> 01:44:53,791
We are the richest people now.

1803
01:44:54,291 --> 01:44:56,708
Hereafter, my name is Johnny Gates.

1804
01:44:57,458 --> 01:44:59,625
Manav, Rosy, find the diamonds.

1805
01:45:01,458 --> 01:45:02,750
Diamonds. Diamonds.

1806
01:45:02,833 --> 01:45:05,041
Hey, this is more
precious than the Kohinoor.

1807
01:45:05,875 --> 01:45:08,333
We will dip these
biscuits in milk and eat.

1808
01:45:08,458 --> 01:45:09,791
What are you waiting for?

1809
01:45:09,958 --> 01:45:11,666
- Grab as much as you can.
- Yes.

1810
01:45:11,875 --> 01:45:16,125
- Take these as well.
- Chocolate, PS5, pizza, we'll buy it all.

1811
01:45:16,833 --> 01:45:18,125
Now, we've become wealthy.

1812
01:45:18,250 --> 01:45:20,208
Mom won't have to work anymore.

1813
01:45:20,375 --> 01:45:22,000
Grab as much as you can.

1814
01:45:22,083 --> 01:45:23,250
Everything is for your mom.

1815
01:45:23,791 --> 01:45:26,250
God! If only we could get a sack now.

1816
01:45:26,375 --> 01:45:27,291
Excuse me!

1817
01:45:27,833 --> 01:45:28,750
A sack.

1818
01:45:29,000 --> 01:45:29,916
A girl by your side,

1819
01:45:30,000 --> 01:45:31,500
and a sack in your hand.
You got lucky.

1820
01:45:31,583 --> 01:45:34,041
- Thank you. Open the sack.
- Yes, yes.

1821
01:45:34,333 --> 01:45:35,208
Hurry up.

1822
01:45:36,375 --> 01:45:38,208
<i>- Bhabhi,</i> a sack.
- Thank you.

1823
01:45:38,291 --> 01:45:40,208
May the evil eyes stay away.

1824
01:45:41,125 --> 01:45:42,916
Santa Claus uncle, take this.

1825
01:45:44,208 --> 01:45:45,250
Thank you, lollipop.

1826
01:45:45,541 --> 01:45:46,583
From where did you get this sack?

1827
01:45:46,875 --> 01:45:47,750
That uncle gave me.

1828
01:45:55,958 --> 01:45:57,208
Hello, friends.

1829
01:45:58,666 --> 01:46:00,458
- Adhoora, you?!
<i>- "Adhoora?"</i>

1830
01:46:02,250 --> 01:46:03,416
But he seems complete.

1831
01:46:03,541 --> 01:46:05,750
Adhoora is back.

1832
01:46:08,000 --> 01:46:11,083
Grab it… grab the treasure for me.

1833
01:46:11,458 --> 01:46:12,333
Come on. Come on.

1834
01:46:13,208 --> 01:46:15,000
Why should we grab it out for you?

1835
01:46:15,708 --> 01:46:17,875
And who are you, crooked walker?

1836
01:46:17,958 --> 01:46:19,041
A finance minister?

1837
01:46:21,125 --> 01:46:22,958
No. A defense minister.

1838
01:46:23,666 --> 01:46:25,666
- Pirates, the gunner.
- Bro…

1839
01:46:26,208 --> 01:46:28,291
Adhoora, how did you reach here?

1840
01:46:34,166 --> 01:46:37,875
Am I putting on a show?
Why are you all clapping?

1841
01:46:38,625 --> 01:46:39,791
Hey, come out.

1842
01:46:45,291 --> 01:46:46,166
Prithvi, you?!

1843
01:46:48,041 --> 01:46:49,083
Prithvi Deshpande?!

1844
01:46:49,250 --> 01:46:50,125
Is he alive?

1845
01:46:50,458 --> 01:46:51,791
This is cheating.

1846
01:46:52,250 --> 01:46:55,250
Every time the one who tells
the secret to the treasure dies.

1847
01:46:55,333 --> 01:46:56,958
The same thing happened
in the last three parts.

1848
01:46:58,041 --> 01:46:58,916
How did you survive?

1849
01:47:00,250 --> 01:47:01,125
I'll tell you.

1850
01:47:01,625 --> 01:47:06,791
Behind the "O".

1851
01:47:39,708 --> 01:47:42,041
Gun shooter G9.

1852
01:47:43,708 --> 01:47:45,708
- Hello!
- Get lost!

1853
01:47:48,875 --> 01:47:51,333
Alright, enough of your story now.

1854
01:47:51,666 --> 01:47:53,375
Go stand in line with the others.

1855
01:47:53,875 --> 01:47:56,125
- How come?
- Do as I say.

1856
01:47:56,208 --> 01:47:58,041
But I'm on your team now.

1857
01:47:58,458 --> 01:47:59,875
I brought you all here.

1858
01:48:00,458 --> 01:48:01,333
Oh really?

1859
01:48:01,583 --> 01:48:03,750
Now, I will send you up

1860
01:48:03,833 --> 01:48:05,583
to the other world. Go there.

1861
01:48:07,041 --> 01:48:09,416
You cheater. If I get
out of this place alive,

1862
01:48:09,666 --> 01:48:11,125
I won't spare you. Hold this.

1863
01:48:11,208 --> 01:48:12,083
Thank you.

1864
01:48:13,833 --> 01:48:14,916
- Give it back!
- Hey!

1865
01:48:15,791 --> 01:48:16,875
Make everyone stand in a line.

1866
01:48:16,958 --> 01:48:18,750
- Everyone, stand in a line.
- Hurry up.

1867
01:48:18,833 --> 01:48:20,250
- Come on. Come on.
- We're already in line.

1868
01:48:20,333 --> 01:48:22,916
- In line. In line, move.
- Come on.

1869
01:48:23,125 --> 01:48:24,125
Ready.

1870
01:48:24,333 --> 01:48:26,041
They came here to loot the treasure.

1871
01:48:31,208 --> 01:48:33,833
Now, whatever items
all of you've grabbed,

1872
01:48:34,375 --> 01:48:36,041
- return everything. Jheenga.
- Yes.

1873
01:48:37,708 --> 01:48:38,583
- Drop it.
- Come on.

1874
01:48:41,458 --> 01:48:42,333
Take that out.

1875
01:48:42,666 --> 01:48:43,875
Chocolates are gone.

1876
01:48:44,000 --> 01:48:45,250
Pizza is gone.

1877
01:48:45,583 --> 01:48:46,708
So is the burger.

1878
01:48:47,208 --> 01:48:48,083
Keep it in here.

1879
01:48:48,791 --> 01:48:49,708
Take it out.

1880
01:48:52,833 --> 01:48:54,166
- Give it.
- I'm sorry. You can go ahead.

1881
01:48:54,250 --> 01:48:55,250
Okay. Hey!

1882
01:48:57,666 --> 01:49:00,291
Wanted to become rich
but turned into idiots.

1883
01:49:00,583 --> 01:49:03,041
Wanted to become billionaires,
instead became beggars.

1884
01:49:03,125 --> 01:49:05,208
You filthy fellow, go to hell!

1885
01:49:08,000 --> 01:49:08,875
Put it back.

1886
01:49:17,708 --> 01:49:19,875
Adi, give back the thing
you've put in your mouth.

1887
01:49:21,250 --> 01:49:22,625
No, Adi. No violence.

1888
01:49:24,208 --> 01:49:25,250
What is it?
Take it out.

1889
01:49:27,958 --> 01:49:28,833
Take it out.

1890
01:49:28,916 --> 01:49:29,791
How much time will you take?

1891
01:49:34,791 --> 01:49:35,666
Hey…

1892
01:49:44,458 --> 01:49:46,666
Take it out. Take it out, quickly.

1893
01:49:46,916 --> 01:49:47,791
You will be cursed.

1894
01:49:47,875 --> 01:49:48,750
No, I won't be.

1895
01:49:51,791 --> 01:49:54,166
We don't use the incense sticks, okay?

1896
01:49:54,583 --> 01:49:55,625
Keep this.

1897
01:49:55,916 --> 01:49:57,250
- Hey, girl, take everything out.
- Come on. Take it out.

1898
01:49:57,708 --> 01:49:58,625
Come on.

1899
01:49:58,750 --> 01:50:01,166
<i>- Bhabhi's </i>bangles.
- May you be ruined!

1900
01:50:01,708 --> 01:50:04,250
May your children
be born squint-eyed.

1901
01:50:04,333 --> 01:50:05,750
- Like this?
- Here you go.

1902
01:50:06,375 --> 01:50:08,916
May you never be at peace in life!

1903
01:50:09,458 --> 01:50:10,583
- Take this, too.
- Wow!

1904
01:50:10,875 --> 01:50:11,916
And what about the one in your wrist?

1905
01:50:12,083 --> 01:50:13,250
That's my personal item.

1906
01:50:13,541 --> 01:50:15,541
We are professional pirates.

1907
01:50:15,708 --> 01:50:17,375
Robbers! Give it.

1908
01:50:17,833 --> 01:50:19,291
Give it. Give it. Give it.

1909
01:50:21,833 --> 01:50:22,875
Who would dare ask her?

1910
01:50:22,958 --> 01:50:24,333
No problem, move ahead.

1911
01:50:27,166 --> 01:50:28,041
Hey, hero!

1912
01:50:29,500 --> 01:50:30,500
- Come on.
- Give away everything.

1913
01:50:35,875 --> 01:50:37,125
Hey, return that.

1914
01:50:40,750 --> 01:50:42,041
You seem very clever.

1915
01:50:42,583 --> 01:50:43,708
Did you switch the sacks?

1916
01:50:43,958 --> 01:50:44,916
What's in your mouth?

1917
01:50:45,541 --> 01:50:46,416
What's in your mouth?

1918
01:50:46,500 --> 01:50:48,083
Hey, what's in your mouth?

1919
01:50:49,791 --> 01:50:50,833
Take it out.

1920
01:50:51,750 --> 01:50:53,125
I said take it out.

1921
01:50:57,166 --> 01:50:58,083
What is this?

1922
01:50:59,166 --> 01:51:00,625
It's betel leaf spit, man.

1923
01:51:01,416 --> 01:51:03,166
It's sweet. Want to taste it?

1924
01:51:03,416 --> 01:51:05,541
Hey, this guy's crazy.
Completely mad.

1925
01:51:06,208 --> 01:51:07,916
He's a psycho. An idiot…

1926
01:51:09,541 --> 01:51:10,500
Yes…

1927
01:51:11,458 --> 01:51:14,541
All this treasure, Jheenga…

1928
01:51:14,625 --> 01:51:15,666
Now, it belongs to me.

1929
01:51:15,833 --> 01:51:17,291
We won't let you take
this treasure away!

1930
01:51:17,375 --> 01:51:19,208
- Hey.
- We won't let you…

1931
01:51:19,583 --> 01:51:20,458
Don't move.

1932
01:51:20,750 --> 01:51:22,125
Get ready to die!

1933
01:51:22,416 --> 01:51:23,958
Kill all of them!

1934
01:51:24,333 --> 01:51:25,291
Gunmen!

1935
01:51:27,125 --> 01:51:28,250
Aim!

1936
01:51:33,833 --> 01:51:34,833
Fire!

1937
01:51:37,458 --> 01:51:38,375
What happened?

1938
01:51:39,583 --> 01:51:40,458
How?

1939
01:51:40,583 --> 01:51:41,541
Jheenga…

1940
01:51:42,875 --> 01:51:43,833
…what happened?

1941
01:51:45,000 --> 01:51:46,625
Boss, that ship had sunk
in the water, right?

1942
01:51:46,708 --> 01:51:48,791
- Yes.
- So, water got inside the guns.

1943
01:51:49,208 --> 01:51:50,708
We didn't have time to repair them.

1944
01:51:51,041 --> 01:51:52,375
And we didn't find any
shop on the way, either.

1945
01:51:52,625 --> 01:51:53,500
Jheenga, you…

1946
01:51:53,625 --> 01:51:54,625
Hey!

1947
01:51:55,250 --> 01:51:57,125
Stop! Stop!

1948
01:51:57,208 --> 01:51:59,250
This is a very powerful bomb.

1949
01:52:00,166 --> 01:52:01,833
- Step back.
- You can't do this.

1950
01:52:01,916 --> 01:52:03,375
I will do it.

1951
01:52:04,750 --> 01:52:07,458
And I'll do exactly this.
No one can stop me.

1952
01:52:07,833 --> 01:52:09,375
- Boss!
- Yes, Jheenga!

1953
01:52:09,458 --> 01:52:10,333
Fire!

1954
01:52:10,416 --> 01:52:13,250
Of course I'll light it before
throwing the bomb at them.

1955
01:52:13,625 --> 01:52:15,416
They'll be blown into pieces.

1956
01:52:15,500 --> 01:52:16,958
Boss, we'll die, too.

1957
01:52:17,041 --> 01:52:19,083
No way, Jheenga.

1958
01:52:19,291 --> 01:52:21,916
I'll throw this bomb over there.
Those idiots will die.

1959
01:52:22,000 --> 01:52:23,291
All of us will die.

1960
01:52:23,375 --> 01:52:27,541
Look, Jheenga, look how they're
begging for their lives.

1961
01:52:27,666 --> 01:52:28,541
Look there.

1962
01:52:28,625 --> 01:52:31,500
Boss, we won't even
be left alive to beg.

1963
01:52:31,625 --> 01:52:32,666
- Jheenga.
- Yes.

1964
01:52:32,750 --> 01:52:34,833
Why do your eyes make it seem

1965
01:52:35,000 --> 01:52:36,583
like I've already lit the bomb?

1966
01:52:36,750 --> 01:52:37,708
Yes, you did.

1967
01:52:38,083 --> 01:52:39,041
You idiot.

1968
01:53:10,666 --> 01:53:12,291
Oh no. It's gone.

1969
01:53:14,125 --> 01:53:15,000
Everything is gone.

1970
01:53:21,000 --> 01:53:22,250
The treasure is gone!

1971
01:53:22,750 --> 01:53:24,375
No, no! Don't go there.

1972
01:53:24,458 --> 01:53:27,458
- The treasure…
- Adi, the treasure is gone.

1973
01:53:30,250 --> 01:53:31,166
Treasure is lost.

1974
01:53:31,458 --> 01:53:32,500
Everything is gone.

1975
01:53:35,833 --> 01:53:36,708
Bro.

1976
01:53:38,208 --> 01:53:39,166
Adhoora!

1977
01:53:39,750 --> 01:53:41,458
- Tell me, Jheenga.
- What should I say?

1978
01:53:41,791 --> 01:53:44,375
Your father gave you the right name.
Adhoora.

1979
01:53:44,541 --> 01:53:46,375
You can never complete any task.

1980
01:53:46,625 --> 01:53:48,583
You're bad luck even for yourself.

1981
01:53:48,666 --> 01:53:52,250
Why don't you jump into
this pit and die, Adhoora?

1982
01:53:53,750 --> 01:53:56,125
Idiot! First you burned the map,

1983
01:53:56,666 --> 01:53:57,875
now you've destroyed
the treasure, too.

1984
01:53:58,208 --> 01:53:59,125
I won't spare you.

1985
01:54:04,750 --> 01:54:06,541
- Run!
- Run!

1986
01:54:17,666 --> 01:54:19,541
This is breaking, bro.

1987
01:54:23,375 --> 01:54:24,291
Oh shit.

1988
01:54:25,333 --> 01:54:27,500
Mom! Mom!

1989
01:54:36,791 --> 01:54:38,916
Move! Move! Run away.

1990
01:54:39,041 --> 01:54:40,583
- Bro!
- Run! Move away!

1991
01:54:45,000 --> 01:54:45,958
Come on. Come on.

1992
01:54:47,541 --> 01:54:48,833
- Run, bro.
- Run, run!

1993
01:54:49,625 --> 01:54:50,500
Run!

1994
01:54:52,791 --> 01:54:54,958
- Come on!
- Hurry up.

1995
01:55:03,208 --> 01:55:04,791
Oh no! Be careful.

1996
01:55:06,250 --> 01:55:07,291
Be careful!

1997
01:55:09,083 --> 01:55:10,916
Come on, kids!

1998
01:55:11,208 --> 01:55:13,000
- Hello, Aaliya.
- Hi, Guddu!

1999
01:55:13,083 --> 01:55:14,541
How's your bonding trip going?

2000
01:55:14,625 --> 01:55:16,833
- Everything is falling apart.
- Give it to me.

2001
01:55:17,125 --> 01:55:18,041
Hello, <i>bhabhi!</i>

2002
01:55:18,666 --> 01:55:20,333
The climax is going on right now.

2003
01:55:20,416 --> 01:55:21,375
Hang up for now.

2004
01:55:21,541 --> 01:55:23,583
Otherwise, along with the hero,

2005
01:55:23,666 --> 01:55:25,583
the supporting cast
will die too, <i>bhabhi!</i>

2006
01:55:28,000 --> 01:55:29,166
Listen, Johnny…

2007
01:55:33,250 --> 01:55:34,250
Careful, Paro!

2008
01:55:47,083 --> 01:55:47,958
Let's jump.

2009
01:55:48,041 --> 01:55:49,916
- Let's jump across.
- No, no…

2010
01:55:50,500 --> 01:55:51,375
I can't do it.

2011
01:55:51,458 --> 01:55:52,750
I won't be able to jump. No.

2012
01:55:52,833 --> 01:55:54,041
You can do it. Come on, jump.

2013
01:55:54,125 --> 01:55:55,583
No, I can't.

2014
01:56:11,375 --> 01:56:12,250
Take this.

2015
01:56:13,166 --> 01:56:14,291
These are the property documents.

2016
01:56:16,458 --> 01:56:17,666
I've already put my thumbprint.

2017
01:56:19,666 --> 01:56:21,083
You'll get 50 lakhs.

2018
01:56:30,708 --> 01:56:31,791
I know…

2019
01:56:33,375 --> 01:56:34,916
…you don't love me.

2020
01:56:37,375 --> 01:56:38,708
I'm just a burden on you.

2021
01:56:41,541 --> 01:56:42,500
So, go…

2022
01:56:43,166 --> 01:56:45,708
Today, I free you from every bond.

2023
01:57:03,208 --> 01:57:06,916
Maybe I'm a little greedy man…

2024
01:57:10,916 --> 01:57:11,958
…but I'm not a coward

2025
01:57:12,041 --> 01:57:13,333
to leave my wife in the

2026
01:57:14,958 --> 01:57:16,250
jaws of death and run away.

2027
01:57:19,416 --> 01:57:21,416
Now, I'll jump only with you.

2028
01:57:22,583 --> 01:57:23,500
No, but…

2029
01:57:23,875 --> 01:57:25,166
How will you carry me?

2030
01:57:26,166 --> 01:57:28,166
When a person becomes
responsible, Paro,

2031
01:57:29,333 --> 01:57:31,125
then no matter how heavy
the responsibility is,

2032
01:57:32,125 --> 01:57:33,166
he carries it somehow.

2033
01:57:35,625 --> 01:57:39,541
Lord Rama crossed the
ocean to save Goddess Sita.

2034
01:57:41,333 --> 01:57:43,375
I also belong to the land of Lord Rama.

2035
01:57:45,666 --> 01:57:47,208
So, can't I at least take

2036
01:57:49,375 --> 01:57:51,041
this small jump to save you?

2037
01:58:07,958 --> 01:58:09,916
Glory to Lord Rama!

2038
01:58:56,208 --> 01:58:58,375
We survived!

2039
01:58:58,875 --> 01:58:59,875
You survived…

2040
01:59:00,583 --> 01:59:01,916
…but I got buried inside.

2041
01:59:08,500 --> 01:59:09,416
Come on. Come on.

2042
01:59:09,916 --> 01:59:11,875
Come fast. Run!

2043
01:59:14,083 --> 01:59:15,583
- Come on.
<i>- Bhabhi!</i>

2044
01:59:15,666 --> 01:59:16,833
Rosy, come fast.

2045
01:59:27,250 --> 01:59:28,208
Oh shit!

2046
01:59:29,083 --> 01:59:29,958
<i>Bhabhi!</i>

2047
01:59:32,000 --> 01:59:34,041
Oh shit, <i>Bhabhi!</i>

2048
01:59:38,583 --> 01:59:41,041
Manav! Manav, please save me.

2049
01:59:41,208 --> 01:59:43,125
<i>Bhabhi,</i> don't panic.

2050
01:59:43,625 --> 01:59:44,916
I'll save you.

2051
01:59:45,666 --> 01:59:46,708
Don't worry.

2052
01:59:47,916 --> 01:59:48,875
I'm there, <i>bhabhi.</i>

2053
01:59:53,708 --> 01:59:56,250
Manav, let go of my hand,

2054
01:59:56,375 --> 01:59:57,791
or you'll fall, too.

2055
01:59:57,916 --> 01:59:58,833
No, <i>bhabhi.</i>

2056
01:59:59,125 --> 02:00:00,083
No matter what happens,

2057
02:00:00,833 --> 02:00:02,541
I won't let go of your hand.

2058
02:00:03,791 --> 02:00:04,750
I won't leave.

2059
02:00:05,083 --> 02:00:06,833
Manav, listen to me.

2060
02:00:06,958 --> 02:00:07,875
No, <i>bhabhi.</i>

2061
02:00:08,291 --> 02:00:09,458
Manav, leave me!

2062
02:00:12,791 --> 02:00:14,208
You will also fall.

2063
02:00:14,875 --> 02:00:15,875
Leave me.

2064
02:00:16,166 --> 02:00:18,208
Mom, please help!

2065
02:00:27,541 --> 02:00:30,666
Manav, don't let go of her.

2066
02:00:32,083 --> 02:00:34,000
Pull up, Adi.

2067
02:00:37,666 --> 02:00:39,875
- Manav, don't let go.
- I won't.

2068
02:00:40,916 --> 02:00:42,708
- Come, bro. Come.
- Come on, kids.

2069
02:00:43,208 --> 02:00:44,208
Come, bro.

2070
02:00:44,625 --> 02:00:45,583
Run faster, kids!

2071
02:00:48,041 --> 02:00:48,916
Aarav.

2072
02:00:49,208 --> 02:00:51,916
Oh Bro!

2073
02:00:52,000 --> 02:00:54,083
- Uncle Johnny!
- Stop!

2074
02:00:58,333 --> 02:00:59,291
Uncle Johnny!

2075
02:01:08,166 --> 02:01:09,041
Bro!

2076
02:01:10,291 --> 02:01:11,375
Uncle Johnny survived!

2077
02:01:11,625 --> 02:01:13,625
- Yes, he survived!
- Johnny Uncle!

2078
02:01:14,500 --> 02:01:15,708
But how will we survive?

2079
02:02:03,875 --> 02:02:06,458
Guddu… now it'll be difficult
for us to survive.

2080
02:02:07,041 --> 02:02:10,291
Not until I'm alive!

2081
02:02:10,500 --> 02:02:12,375
Guddu, please save us.

2082
02:02:14,250 --> 02:02:15,958
Both of you will have to trust me.

2083
02:02:17,166 --> 02:02:18,541
- Okay?
- Yes.

2084
02:02:19,041 --> 02:02:19,916
Yes.

2085
02:02:20,708 --> 02:02:21,666
Close your eyes.

2086
02:02:23,458 --> 02:02:26,041
Johnny!

2087
02:02:31,291 --> 02:02:32,750
Catch her.

2088
02:02:52,750 --> 02:02:53,625
Are you okay?

2089
02:02:54,208 --> 02:02:55,125
Thank you!

2090
02:02:55,833 --> 02:02:56,708
Bro!

2091
02:02:57,750 --> 02:03:00,833
- Come on, quickly.
- No, Guddu, no… No. I'll die.

2092
02:03:01,958 --> 02:03:02,875
No, Guddu!

2093
02:03:03,791 --> 02:03:05,666
Guddu, please!

2094
02:03:06,250 --> 02:03:07,750
- Save me, please.
- Bro!

2095
02:03:08,416 --> 02:03:09,791
Help me! Help me!

2096
02:03:13,500 --> 02:03:14,875
Guddu, I don't want to die.

2097
02:03:14,958 --> 02:03:16,375
Nothing will happen to you.

2098
02:03:22,791 --> 02:03:24,333
- Save me.
- Careful!

2099
02:03:25,291 --> 02:03:26,208
Come up, son.

2100
02:03:29,250 --> 02:03:30,541
- Aarav.
- Bro!

2101
02:03:30,625 --> 02:03:31,500
Guddu!

2102
02:03:45,333 --> 02:03:46,958
What are you doing?
Come on.

2103
02:03:47,291 --> 02:03:49,000
No, Guddu.
No, I can't do this.

2104
02:03:49,250 --> 02:03:50,416
- I will die.
- Shut up.

2105
02:03:51,541 --> 02:03:52,583
Nothing will happen to you.

2106
02:03:53,916 --> 02:03:54,791
Trust me, please.

2107
02:03:55,875 --> 02:03:56,750
Please, son.

2108
02:03:57,291 --> 02:03:58,166
Come on.

2109
02:04:04,458 --> 02:04:06,041
Come, my brave boy.

2110
02:04:17,041 --> 02:04:17,916
Get up.

2111
02:04:18,666 --> 02:04:19,541
Get up.

2112
02:04:22,041 --> 02:04:24,083
Bro, you also come down now.

2113
02:04:24,291 --> 02:04:25,208
Come, Guddu!

2114
02:04:25,500 --> 02:04:26,375
Come on!

2115
02:04:27,083 --> 02:04:28,416
- Bro!
- Guddu!

2116
02:04:28,541 --> 02:04:29,416
Guddu!

2117
02:04:30,625 --> 02:04:31,500
Guddu!

2118
02:04:31,916 --> 02:04:34,125
- Bro!
- Guddu, careful!

2119
02:04:34,666 --> 02:04:36,125
Come on!

2120
02:04:36,208 --> 02:04:37,333
- Bro!
- Guddu!

2121
02:04:38,208 --> 02:04:39,166
Guddu!

2122
02:05:09,625 --> 02:05:11,333
Guddu!

2123
02:05:15,041 --> 02:05:15,958
- Are you alright?
- Yes.

2124
02:05:20,458 --> 02:05:23,166
I'll lose some weight, okay.

2125
02:05:27,583 --> 02:05:28,500
Paro,

2126
02:05:29,833 --> 02:05:31,916
you need not lose weight.

2127
02:05:33,875 --> 02:05:37,041
I will let go of my greed.

2128
02:05:40,458 --> 02:05:42,250
- I'm sorry, Paro.
- What are you doing?

2129
02:05:43,041 --> 02:05:45,208
Don't do that.
You're my husband.

2130
02:05:45,791 --> 02:05:47,000
You're like my God.

2131
02:05:56,166 --> 02:05:57,125
Are you alright?

2132
02:06:01,833 --> 02:06:02,833
Thank you, Manav.

2133
02:06:02,916 --> 02:06:03,958
Welcome, <i>bhabhi.</i>

2134
02:06:06,583 --> 02:06:07,500
Well,

2135
02:06:08,333 --> 02:06:09,500
you had told me that

2136
02:06:10,750 --> 02:06:13,000
before this trip ends,
I'll have to make a decision.

2137
02:06:20,375 --> 02:06:21,541
My decision is that…

2138
02:06:24,958 --> 02:06:26,375
I can't live without Manav.

2139
02:06:30,208 --> 02:06:31,166
I'm sorry.

2140
02:06:32,458 --> 02:06:34,083
Send me the divorce papers.
I'll sign them.

2141
02:06:37,541 --> 02:06:38,458
Let's go, Manav.

2142
02:06:38,708 --> 02:06:39,625
No, Adi,

2143
02:06:41,166 --> 02:06:42,458
if we leave her behind,

2144
02:06:42,875 --> 02:06:44,500
Mom won't be proud of us.

2145
02:06:47,916 --> 02:06:48,875
Let's go, Manav.

2146
02:06:49,583 --> 02:06:50,708
No, Adi, I won't go.

2147
02:06:52,083 --> 02:06:52,958
Let's go, Manav.

2148
02:06:53,041 --> 02:06:53,916
- No.
- Adi!

2149
02:06:56,500 --> 02:06:57,458
I'm sorry.

2150
02:06:58,875 --> 02:06:59,958
I'm really sorry.

2151
02:07:02,125 --> 02:07:03,500
I've realized

2152
02:07:04,708 --> 02:07:06,458
that family members
don't need to be perfect.

2153
02:07:08,458 --> 02:07:09,833
They just need to have
love for each other.

2154
02:07:15,375 --> 02:07:16,625
I'm sorry, Manav!

2155
02:07:17,791 --> 02:07:20,541
<i>Bhabhi,</i> why are you apologizing?

2156
02:07:21,458 --> 02:07:22,666
I should be the one apologizing.

2157
02:07:22,750 --> 02:07:23,708
No… What are you doing?

2158
02:07:23,791 --> 02:07:25,291
- Get up!
- Hey, man.

2159
02:07:25,375 --> 02:07:26,333
Oh shit.

2160
02:07:27,333 --> 02:07:29,416
What have you done?
You broke her nose.

2161
02:07:30,666 --> 02:07:31,541
What?

2162
02:07:31,791 --> 02:07:32,666
It's okay.

2163
02:07:32,958 --> 02:07:33,833
Sorry.

2164
02:07:33,916 --> 02:07:35,208
- It's okay.
- Sorry. Sorry.

2165
02:07:39,125 --> 02:07:40,625
I'll get used to Manav.

2166
02:07:42,666 --> 02:07:45,541
See, even <i>bhabhi </i>likes me.

2167
02:07:45,833 --> 02:07:46,791
Yes.

2168
02:07:49,875 --> 02:07:50,833
Let's go.

2169
02:07:54,041 --> 02:07:57,541
Guddu sacrificed his life
to save you two.

2170
02:07:59,625 --> 02:08:00,541
Had dad been alive,

2171
02:08:00,625 --> 02:08:01,833
he too would've done
the same thing, right?

2172
02:08:02,958 --> 02:08:07,291
Sister, our family has
become incomplete again.

2173
02:08:11,916 --> 02:08:12,875
Yes, Aarav,

2174
02:08:13,666 --> 02:08:15,500
once again we lost our father.

2175
02:08:16,750 --> 02:08:19,000
Yes, sister. We lost him.

2176
02:08:21,583 --> 02:08:22,916
What if he's still alive?

2177
02:08:23,500 --> 02:08:26,583
Who would survive this fall?

2178
02:08:27,416 --> 02:08:28,375
He can survive.

2179
02:08:29,375 --> 02:08:30,583
Because he's Guddu.

2180
02:08:31,208 --> 02:08:32,166
And not any weak fellow.

2181
02:08:39,791 --> 02:08:40,833
Guddu!

2182
02:08:52,458 --> 02:08:53,791
Guddu, I love you.

2183
02:08:53,875 --> 02:08:55,208
Aarav, behave.

2184
02:08:55,375 --> 02:08:56,291
Don't call him Guddu.

2185
02:08:56,708 --> 02:08:58,208
- Call him dad.
- Yes.

2186
02:08:59,083 --> 02:09:00,125
I love you all, too.

2187
02:09:06,416 --> 02:09:08,916
The treasure was right in our hands, bro.
And now it's gone.

2188
02:09:09,333 --> 02:09:11,250
No… I got two diamonds instead.

2189
02:09:11,416 --> 02:09:13,083
- Where?
- Where are they? Show me.

2190
02:09:13,750 --> 02:09:15,666
When a person finds his family,

2191
02:09:17,125 --> 02:09:18,708
there's no treasure greater than that.

2192
02:09:19,333 --> 02:09:20,625
I found these two precious diamonds.

2193
02:09:21,083 --> 02:09:23,375
And we also found our hero.
That's you.

2194
02:09:24,666 --> 02:09:25,791
So true, Guddu.

2195
02:09:26,333 --> 02:09:28,458
I was also blindly running
after the treasure all my life.

2196
02:09:28,958 --> 02:09:32,500
I never realized that the
real treasure is with me.

2197
02:09:32,791 --> 02:09:33,666
Yes.

2198
02:09:34,208 --> 02:09:36,500
The real treasure is always our family.

2199
02:09:36,958 --> 02:09:37,833
Yes.

2200
02:09:37,916 --> 02:09:39,416
My <i>bhabhi </i>is back.

2201
02:09:39,666 --> 02:09:41,833
Adi is no longer a widower.

2202
02:09:41,916 --> 02:09:44,333
Not a widower.
You can say I am still married.

2203
02:09:44,416 --> 02:09:45,333
It's the same thing.

2204
02:09:45,416 --> 02:09:46,375
Let's quickly go home now.

2205
02:09:46,458 --> 02:09:48,000
I want to relish the parathas
made by <i>bhabhi.</i>

2206
02:09:48,416 --> 02:09:50,208
- Let's go.
- But how do we go home?

2207
02:09:50,666 --> 02:09:51,541
Yes.

2208
02:09:52,791 --> 02:09:53,666
Look there.

2209
02:09:59,541 --> 02:10:01,750
- That's a ship.
- Yes, a ship.

2210
02:10:02,125 --> 02:10:03,583
We'll make it!

2211
02:10:06,125 --> 02:10:07,208
We'll make it.

2212
02:10:09,833 --> 02:10:10,833
Oh shit!

2213
02:10:11,166 --> 02:10:13,000
- What happened?
- We're not safe. We're dead.

2214
02:10:13,583 --> 02:10:14,708
Look whose ship it is.

2215
02:10:19,791 --> 02:10:24,125
The incomplete man, bro!
Adhoora returns!

2216
02:10:35,750 --> 02:10:36,666
Don't be scared.

2217
02:10:37,500 --> 02:10:38,625
I'm not a villain anymore.

2218
02:10:39,875 --> 02:10:45,541
I've come to understand that
the world loves heroes, not villains.

2219
02:10:45,916 --> 02:10:50,000
Guddu saved my life. That's why
I've given up the pirate life.

2220
02:10:50,583 --> 02:10:52,083
- That's great.
- Amazing!

2221
02:10:53,000 --> 02:10:55,083
I'd heard that Munna Bhai
had given up his gangster life.

2222
02:10:55,416 --> 02:10:57,541
This is the first time I've seen
someone give up the pirate life.

2223
02:10:58,208 --> 02:10:59,458
- Wow!
- Also…

2224
02:11:00,166 --> 02:11:03,125
from now on, this ship is my tourist boat.

2225
02:11:03,958 --> 02:11:05,541
You guys are the first ones aboard.

2226
02:11:05,833 --> 02:11:07,125
- Wow!
- Good!

2227
02:11:07,250 --> 02:11:08,916
Adi, what do I do with this?

2228
02:11:09,000 --> 02:11:10,041
Incense? Just throw it out.

2229
02:11:10,791 --> 02:11:11,666
Stop!

2230
02:11:22,375 --> 02:11:24,041
One more map, bro?

2231
02:11:26,583 --> 02:11:28,875
This looks like a map to a huge treasure.

2232
02:11:29,791 --> 02:11:30,958
Who's going to decode it?

2233
02:11:31,083 --> 02:11:32,000
Hello!

2234
02:11:34,625 --> 02:11:36,625
I will do it. Don't worry.

2235
02:11:36,708 --> 02:11:37,625
You?!

2236
02:11:37,958 --> 02:11:38,875
You are still alive?!

2237
02:11:39,000 --> 02:11:39,875
Yeah.

2238
02:11:40,041 --> 02:11:42,166
You've escaped death so many times,
you should've died of shame by now!

2239
02:11:42,458 --> 02:11:44,250
What do I do?
I just don't feel any shame.

2240
02:11:44,833 --> 02:11:46,000
I'll decode it. Yeah.

2241
02:11:46,375 --> 02:11:47,375
Come on.

2242
02:11:50,500 --> 02:11:51,375
Bring it here.

2243
02:11:53,291 --> 02:11:54,166
Oh!

2244
02:15:03,291 --> 02:15:04,250
{\an8}CHATNI

2245
02:15:21,166 --> 02:15:23,083
{\an8}Roll camera and action!

2246
02:15:29,208 --> 02:15:30,125
{\an8}Hey!

2247
02:15:30,208 --> 02:15:31,791
{\an8}Adi, they are shooting something.

2248
02:15:32,916 --> 02:15:34,208
{\an8}How are they shooting without us?

2249
02:15:34,333 --> 02:15:35,291
{\an8}This is our song.

2250
02:15:36,333 --> 02:15:37,291
{\an8}- Yeah, come on.
- Let's go.

2251
02:15:37,416 --> 02:15:38,583
{\an8}They're shooting <i>Dhamaal</i> without us?